WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:02.953
Provided by explosiveskull


00:00:03.561 --> 00:00:04.761
OK!


00:00:05.329 --> 00:00:07.365
Don't know how many of you
are new and how many of you


00:00:07.398 --> 00:00:08.532
have been with us
from the start,


00:00:08.566 --> 00:00:11.335
but I am Laura Hollis.


00:00:11.369 --> 00:00:13.903
<i>Yes, the Laura Hollis</i>


00:00:13.937 --> 00:00:15.373
who recently got famous, or...


00:00:15.406 --> 00:00:16.906
"internet famous"


00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:18.208
because my university pals and I


00:00:18.241 --> 00:00:20.243
vlogged ourselves
saving the world.


00:00:25.349 --> 00:00:27.318
See, back in my freshman year,
we discovered


00:00:27.351 --> 00:00:29.487
that our Austrian university
was actually being


00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:32.055
run by an evil dean
and her vampire cult.


00:00:32.088 --> 00:00:34.157
Naturally.


00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:36.226
They'd been sacrificing girls
to this...


00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.228
monstrous creature
under the campus


00:00:38.262 --> 00:00:40.196
for centuries, and I was next.


00:00:41.599 --> 00:00:43.434
Really should've
gone to that safety school.


00:00:44.602 --> 00:00:47.538
Anyway....
The dean sent Carmilla.


00:00:47.571 --> 00:00:49.473
I'm your new roommate,
sweetheart.


00:00:49.507 --> 00:00:51.542
A 300-year old vampire


00:00:51.575 --> 00:00:53.544
with a checkered past


00:00:53.577 --> 00:00:56.246
and centuries worth of victims
to kidnap me.


00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.015
<i>There was just one little snag
with that plan.</i>


00:01:01.951 --> 00:01:03.820
Carm and I fell in love.


00:01:05.456 --> 00:01:07.591
Carm turned her back
on the evil dean,


00:01:07.625 --> 00:01:10.093
and with a little help
from our friends,


00:01:10.126 --> 00:01:12.896
Laf, Perry, Kirsch,


00:01:12.929 --> 00:01:15.466
Mel and Danny,
we saved the school...


00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:18.569
...and the world.


00:01:18.602 --> 00:01:20.571
For stopping the apocalypse,
Carm earned herself


00:01:20.604 --> 00:01:23.307
a magical, human life.
A vampire no more!


00:01:23.341 --> 00:01:25.276
A chance to...


00:01:25.309 --> 00:01:28.446
start again and leave
the crimes of her past behind,


00:01:28.479 --> 00:01:30.481
and for us to figure out...


00:01:33.149 --> 00:01:34.618
...whatever happens next.


00:01:56.379 --> 00:01:57.380
OK...


00:01:58.381 --> 00:02:00.048
Weird.


00:02:05.086 --> 00:02:06.722
Old-timey and weird.


00:02:26.409 --> 00:02:27.410
Hello?


00:02:33.783 --> 00:02:35.585
Ghost lady?


00:02:52.768 --> 00:02:55.203
- You're wearing my brooch.
- Oh, Carm!


00:02:55.237 --> 00:02:58.139
Did I scare you, my pet?


00:02:58.173 --> 00:03:01.209
You think, sneaking around
dressed like Lizzie Borden?


00:03:01.243 --> 00:03:02.745
Wait...


00:03:02.778 --> 00:03:04.413
Why are you dressed
like Lizzie Borden?


00:03:04.447 --> 00:03:06.549
You mustn't be afraid.


00:03:06.582 --> 00:03:08.584
Why would I be afraid?


00:03:08.618 --> 00:03:12.020
We shall die as lovers may.


00:03:14.222 --> 00:03:16.224
Die together...


00:03:19.094 --> 00:03:21.330
...so that we may live together.


00:03:33.543 --> 00:03:35.745
Welcome back, Cream Puff.


00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.482
I think your horror movies
are giving me nightmares.


00:03:40.483 --> 00:03:41.651
Oh, well...


00:03:41.684 --> 00:03:44.754
Life's rough
like that sometimes.


00:03:48.323 --> 00:03:49.659
Come on!


00:03:49.692 --> 00:03:52.294
How long does it take
to kill one limping teenager?


00:03:52.328 --> 00:03:54.630
Is this guy on a coffee break?


00:03:54.664 --> 00:03:55.698
<i>Get in the car!</i>


00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:01.136
So, what happened?
Did you get scooped up


00:04:01.169 --> 00:04:03.238
by that talking goat again?


00:04:03.271 --> 00:04:05.775
No. I dreamed you
were a vampire.


00:04:08.344 --> 00:04:10.312
It was very...


00:04:10.346 --> 00:04:13.148
blast from your
gothic horror past.


00:04:13.181 --> 00:04:15.384
There was this old house,
and then you...


00:04:17.587 --> 00:04:19.455
...then you were actually
kind of scary.


00:04:19.488 --> 00:04:21.357
I hurt you?


00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:23.359
In a dream.


00:04:23.392 --> 00:04:26.194
Come on, it was probably a...
subconscious fascination


00:04:26.227 --> 00:04:27.863
with Victorian murders.


00:04:29.699 --> 00:04:33.234
- Or, uh... corsets.
- Mmm!


00:04:36.572 --> 00:04:39.675
Well, no need to go
digging around in the past.


00:04:39.709 --> 00:04:41.711
We have it much better now.


00:04:43.379 --> 00:04:44.880
No arguments here.


00:04:46.882 --> 00:04:48.517
So long, hammer horror!


00:04:48.551 --> 00:04:50.886
Hello, rom-com.


00:06:38.728 --> 00:06:40.830
How now, brown cow.


00:06:40.863 --> 00:06:42.832
How now, brown cow!


00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:46.802
Happy anniversary,
faithful viewers!


00:06:46.836 --> 00:06:48.871
I know. I know, I know, I know.


00:06:48.904 --> 00:06:50.840
I'm behind on my posts,


00:06:50.873 --> 00:06:52.742
but I would never miss this,


00:06:52.775 --> 00:06:55.044
because five years ago today,


00:06:55.077 --> 00:06:57.312
<i>a rag-tag bunch of
undergraduates stopped the dean</i>


00:06:57.346 --> 00:07:00.449
<i>of their evil university
from unleashing hell on earth!</i>


00:07:00.483 --> 00:07:03.719
Or... mostly stopped. You can't
really blame us for Antarctica.


00:07:03.753 --> 00:07:06.388
And where are they now,
you might ask?


00:07:06.422 --> 00:07:07.823
Well, let's check in


00:07:07.857 --> 00:07:10.526
with a very special
five-year retrospective.


00:07:13.529 --> 00:07:16.332
And then we will cut to...


00:07:23.439 --> 00:07:25.508
First up is Lafontaine
and Perry, who,


00:07:25.541 --> 00:07:28.010
<i>as you'll recall, transferred
to occult studies at Berkeley</i>


00:07:28.043 --> 00:07:30.012
<i>and then started Laferry
Industries, where they've</i>


00:07:30.045 --> 00:07:32.615
<i>been revolutionizing
life with the supernatural</i>


00:07:32.648 --> 00:07:34.717
<i>with products like their hemo-
soy vegan vampire supplements</i>


00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:37.486
<i>ever since. They've got
this huge meeting</i>


00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:39.488
<i>with a megacorporation that
wants to buy their start-up.</i>


00:07:39.522 --> 00:07:41.490
<i>I'm so proud!</i>


00:07:41.524 --> 00:07:44.360
Speaking of super-successful
people, you guys remember Danny,


00:07:44.393 --> 00:07:46.495
my lit TA turned stalwart ally


00:07:46.529 --> 00:07:48.464
turned repentant vampire


00:07:48.497 --> 00:07:51.367
<i>has turned into...
a vampire rights advocate.</i>


00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.536
And what retrospective
would be complete


00:07:53.569 --> 00:07:55.538
without a look at
how Mel and Kirsch and I


00:07:55.571 --> 00:07:57.673
leveraged our amateur coverage
of the almost apocalypse


00:07:57.706 --> 00:07:59.608
<i>into a career in local news.</i>


00:07:59.642 --> 00:08:02.945
<i>And if you're morbidly curious,
here are some clips!</i>


00:08:02.978 --> 00:08:04.880
Today, we explore the fast-paced


00:08:04.914 --> 00:08:06.782
world of floral arrangements.


00:08:06.816 --> 00:08:09.018
Cranberry bannock.
Ceramic cephalopod.


00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.054
So... yeah.


00:08:12.087 --> 00:08:14.757
I've not quite
achieved Lois Lane-dom.


00:08:15.758 --> 00:08:16.859
But never fear!


00:08:24.133 --> 00:08:26.735
It is all part
of my five-year plan.


00:08:34.109 --> 00:08:35.911
Yeah. Um...


00:08:35.945 --> 00:08:38.647
after Carm and I took
our glorious gap year,


00:08:38.681 --> 00:08:41.851
it was time to start real life.
So, we moved home to TO.


00:08:41.884 --> 00:08:44.687
I finished my degree,
stuck my foot in the door.


00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:46.488
Now, I'm just waiting
for my big break,


00:08:46.522 --> 00:08:48.958
busting open some huge Woodward
and Bernstein-style scandal


00:08:48.991 --> 00:08:50.626
and being moved up
to the city desk.


00:08:51.961 --> 00:08:53.662
Admittedly, I have been...


00:08:53.696 --> 00:08:56.498
waiting a while for that one.


00:08:56.532 --> 00:08:58.100
But, uh, you know,
that's what you do in life.


00:08:58.133 --> 00:08:58.834
You pay your dues.


00:09:00.636 --> 00:09:03.906
Unless you're a former vampire
with 300 years of sunshine


00:09:03.939 --> 00:09:05.975
and culinary history
to catch up on.


00:09:06.976 --> 00:09:08.744
So, what has our Carm been up to


00:09:08.777 --> 00:09:10.880
as a living, breathing human?


00:09:10.913 --> 00:09:13.682
<i>She's definitely taking
advantage of ye olde</i>


00:09:13.716 --> 00:09:15.684
<i>vampire trust fund.</i>


00:09:15.718 --> 00:09:17.753
<i>Bakery-based gluttony: check.</i>


00:09:18.754 --> 00:09:20.522
<i>Sun-tanning sloth: check.</i>


00:09:21.624 --> 00:09:23.993
<i>I-have-a-pulse-now lust.</i>


00:09:25.661 --> 00:09:27.129
<i>Well...</i>


00:09:29.632 --> 00:09:32.001
<i>Actually, I can't really
complain about that last one.</i>


00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.805
Yeah.


00:09:36.839 --> 00:09:39.074
Unless you count
starring in my spooky dreams,


00:09:39.108 --> 00:09:41.810
it's been a bit more pastry
than purpose lately.


00:09:41.844 --> 00:09:43.979
But... today's retrospective


00:09:44.013 --> 00:09:46.048
is all about perspective.


00:09:46.081 --> 00:09:48.117
We are going to get our heroine
back on track.


00:09:49.685 --> 00:09:52.154
But... where to start
such a conversation?


00:09:52.187 --> 00:09:53.756
Where else?


00:09:57.259 --> 00:09:59.762
With dessert! Ha ha!


00:09:59.795 --> 00:10:01.196
Mmm...


00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:03.132
Have you been baking?


00:10:03.165 --> 00:10:05.134
Happy re-birthday!


00:10:09.872 --> 00:10:11.540
It's a...


00:10:11.573 --> 00:10:12.942
like a...
like a birthday,


00:10:12.975 --> 00:10:14.843
but for your rebirth...


00:10:14.877 --> 00:10:16.178
because...


00:10:16.211 --> 00:10:17.880
five years ago,
you got a life.


00:10:17.913 --> 00:10:20.649
Not like a '90s "Get a life!"
but you know, um...


00:10:20.683 --> 00:10:23.118
- Literally.
- Hm.


00:10:23.152 --> 00:10:25.154
How very Lewis Carroll.


00:10:30.826 --> 00:10:32.027
So...


00:10:32.061 --> 00:10:33.729
speaking of five years,


00:10:33.762 --> 00:10:35.698
I was thinking that we
could talk about five years


00:10:35.731 --> 00:10:37.066
in the other direction.


00:10:38.734 --> 00:10:40.736
'Cause you've been
through a lot.


00:10:42.071 --> 00:10:44.606
Not just Silas,
but... death.


00:10:45.607 --> 00:10:47.576
And the French Revolution.


00:10:47.609 --> 00:10:50.012
So... it's completely
understandable that you're


00:10:50.045 --> 00:10:53.048
- feeling a little lost.
- Lost?


00:10:53.082 --> 00:10:55.784
OK, maybe not lost, but...


00:10:55.818 --> 00:10:57.086
maybe a little...


00:10:58.253 --> 00:10:59.621
...aimless.


00:10:59.655 --> 00:11:01.890
Laura, are you
staging an intervention


00:11:01.924 --> 00:11:03.692
because you think
I'm wasting my life?


00:11:03.726 --> 00:11:04.693
No!


00:11:05.761 --> 00:11:06.795
Maybe.


00:11:06.829 --> 00:11:08.097
It's just...


00:11:09.765 --> 00:11:11.934
You aren't immortal anymore.


00:11:11.967 --> 00:11:13.802
And I know that you
want to make the most


00:11:13.836 --> 00:11:16.071
- of our lives together...
- Is there something wrong


00:11:16.105 --> 00:11:18.107
with those lives being fun?


00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:20.242
No...


00:11:20.275 --> 00:11:22.878
but I think it's possible
to have fun and...


00:11:22.911 --> 00:11:25.547
And did I go to that
supernatural therapist?


00:11:25.581 --> 00:11:27.249
One time.


00:11:27.282 --> 00:11:28.817
You said you couldn't
take advice


00:11:28.851 --> 00:11:30.619
from someone born
after the moon landing.


00:11:30.652 --> 00:11:31.520
Mhm.


00:11:32.788 --> 00:11:34.623
And do I pester you
because you would rather


00:11:34.656 --> 00:11:37.059
spend your days
in a news cubicle


00:11:37.092 --> 00:11:39.762
instead of on a beach
in the South of France?


00:11:39.795 --> 00:11:42.031
No, you don't. It's just...


00:11:42.064 --> 00:11:43.966
It's just...


00:11:43.999 --> 00:11:46.802
you like making plans,


00:11:46.835 --> 00:11:49.071
and I love that about you.


00:11:51.073 --> 00:11:53.075
But...


00:11:53.108 --> 00:11:55.711
I don't know.
It's my re-birthday.


00:11:55.744 --> 00:11:58.113
So...


00:11:58.147 --> 00:12:01.050
I wanna spend it
enjoying our lives.


00:12:01.083 --> 00:12:03.018
Preferably...


00:12:03.052 --> 00:12:05.954
somewhere with a... patio


00:12:05.988 --> 00:12:08.123
and an extensive wine selection.


00:12:14.163 --> 00:12:16.265
And chocolates.


00:13:12.788 --> 00:13:13.822
Carm?


00:13:16.225 --> 00:13:17.893
Shh...


00:13:18.894 --> 00:13:20.162
You're dreaming.


00:13:27.769 --> 00:13:28.770
Oh.


00:13:29.771 --> 00:13:30.772
Right.


00:13:37.447 --> 00:13:39.449
You are mine.


00:13:39.482 --> 00:13:41.683
You shall be mine.


00:13:42.718 --> 00:13:45.821
You and I are one...


00:13:46.788 --> 00:13:47.789
...forever.


00:13:49.258 --> 00:13:51.427
Something tells me
I'm gonna like this dream.


00:14:07.943 --> 00:14:09.778
CARM! What are you doing?!


00:14:09.811 --> 00:14:11.246
CARM!


00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:13.282
Hey! Hey!
It's me! It's me!


00:14:16.018 --> 00:14:17.986
Laura, your neck...


00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:19.221
Oh, God!


00:14:31.334 --> 00:14:33.302
What is going on?


00:14:37.139 --> 00:14:39.308
Have you been in close
proximity to any vampires


00:14:39.342 --> 00:14:42.311
or vampire by-products
in the past two or three months?


00:14:42.345 --> 00:14:44.813
Oh, you mean when a Sumerian
goddess turned me again


00:14:44.846 --> 00:14:46.949
last week? Must've
slipped my mind.


00:14:46.982 --> 00:14:48.951
I see the sarcasm
hasn't suffered.


00:14:48.984 --> 00:14:51.119
Thanks for taking time out
of your meeting prep to help us.


00:14:52.455 --> 00:14:54.056
- For you guys... anything.
- Of course.


00:14:54.089 --> 00:14:56.124
We're probably over-prepared.


00:14:56.158 --> 00:14:58.361
Something's definitely off
with Carm.


00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:02.297
For those of us
without a fancy cyborg eye?


00:15:02.332 --> 00:15:03.832
Right. Um...


00:15:05.167 --> 00:15:09.304
This is Carm, and she's,
well, dead except...


00:15:09.339 --> 00:15:11.507
Except the resurrection spell
is still running inside her,


00:15:11.541 --> 00:15:13.842
- making her a living human.
- It makes her heart beat,


00:15:13.875 --> 00:15:15.478
hair grow, and all
the other things


00:15:15.511 --> 00:15:18.481
- a regular human body does.
- Yeah, like a magic battery.


00:15:18.514 --> 00:15:20.483
I thought we agreed
we wouldn't call it that.


00:15:20.516 --> 00:15:22.050
My vote's still
with "life force".


00:15:22.084 --> 00:15:24.152
- No, that's even worse.
- Ooh! What about, um,


00:15:24.186 --> 00:15:26.822
- what about your spark?
- Hm! Does pretty much work


00:15:26.855 --> 00:15:28.857
- like an ignition.
- Spark it is!


00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:30.859
- Spark, spark, spark!
- I hope


00:15:30.892 --> 00:15:32.060
you're enjoying yourselves.


00:15:33.195 --> 00:15:34.229
Uh...


00:15:35.897 --> 00:15:37.433
Carmilla's spark is going out.


00:15:37.467 --> 00:15:40.436
- What's wrong with it?
- It's producing a sort


00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:42.472
of electrical discharge
that's making it flicker,


00:15:42.505 --> 00:15:45.040
and since it's
what's keeping her human,


00:15:45.073 --> 00:15:47.477
- when it flickers, she...
- Vamps out.


00:15:50.112 --> 00:15:51.113
OK, so...


00:15:52.548 --> 00:15:53.915
How do we get my...


00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:58.120
..."spark" to stop flickering?


00:15:58.153 --> 00:16:00.188
We'll have to run
some more tests.


00:16:00.222 --> 00:16:03.258
And in the meantime, Carm just
keeps randomly vamping out?


00:16:03.292 --> 00:16:05.227
What are we supposed
to do about that?


00:16:21.076 --> 00:16:22.911
Ow!


00:16:42.632 --> 00:16:44.567
First of all, she's jazzed.


00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:46.268
Like, "Oh, there'll be
blueberry pie, right?


00:16:46.301 --> 00:16:47.936
I'm into the bluebs."
And then to top it all off,


00:16:47.969 --> 00:16:49.439
I get to the fridge,
and he's just...


00:16:51.273 --> 00:16:52.375
Carm?


00:16:54.544 --> 00:16:56.945
You OK?


00:16:56.978 --> 00:17:00.215
Sure, just... grappling
with an aversion to daylight


00:17:00.248 --> 00:17:01.950
and cravings for blood.


00:17:01.983 --> 00:17:03.419
Hey...


00:17:03.453 --> 00:17:05.421
Laf is gonna
figure something out.


00:17:05.455 --> 00:17:07.989
I know, it's just...


00:17:08.023 --> 00:17:10.092
this was supposed
to be done.


00:17:10.125 --> 00:17:11.960
You know...


00:17:11.993 --> 00:17:15.263
the bloodlust,
the self-loathing,


00:17:15.297 --> 00:17:17.633
the sleeping tied to a chair
in my own bedroom.


00:17:17.667 --> 00:17:19.935
That one might be overkill.


00:17:23.004 --> 00:17:25.441
You've never had a problem
controlling yourself before.


00:17:28.143 --> 00:17:30.112
Unless you count
dream Carm chasing me


00:17:30.145 --> 00:17:32.348
through discount
Transylvania all...


00:17:32.382 --> 00:17:34.484
"You are mine.
You shall be mine."


00:17:36.151 --> 00:17:37.319
Wait. What did you just say?


00:17:38.488 --> 00:17:40.322
"You are mine.
You shall be mine.


00:17:40.356 --> 00:17:42.924
You and I are
one forever."


00:17:48.498 --> 00:17:50.366
Carm, what is going on?


00:17:51.534 --> 00:17:53.369
It was just some
silly Dracu-poetry


00:17:53.403 --> 00:17:55.371
my brain coughed up
for atmosphere.


00:17:58.173 --> 00:18:00.142
What are you looking for?


00:18:06.516 --> 00:18:08.016
That house.


00:18:08.049 --> 00:18:09.652
This is where
Elle and I lived.


00:18:11.654 --> 00:18:13.188
Was this the manor
in your dreams?


00:18:17.393 --> 00:18:19.662
<i>So this place Laura's been
dreaming about, the manor,</i>


00:18:19.695 --> 00:18:21.564
- it's real?
- Not just the manor.


00:18:23.198 --> 00:18:25.635
Carm thinks that,
from what I'm describing,


00:18:25.668 --> 00:18:27.336
the house, the clothes,
what she says -


00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:30.005
that I'm dreaming things
that really happened...


00:18:31.006 --> 00:18:33.141
...150 years ago...


00:18:34.142 --> 00:18:35.043
...to Elle.


00:18:39.214 --> 00:18:40.416
Am I supposed to know
who Elle is?


00:18:41.651 --> 00:18:43.519
Elle, the girl Carm
turned on her mother


00:18:43.553 --> 00:18:44.687
and stopped being evil for?


00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:46.456
That wasn't Laura?


00:18:46.489 --> 00:18:48.624
Carmilla's epic first love?


00:18:48.658 --> 00:18:50.693
Also not Laura?


00:18:50.726 --> 00:18:53.061
Remember our first year
at Silas, those weird dreams


00:18:53.094 --> 00:18:55.063
- I was having?
- Only they weren't dreams,


00:18:55.096 --> 00:18:56.732
they were warnings
from Carm's...


00:19:01.036 --> 00:19:02.672
So you think the dreams
are from Elle?


00:19:02.705 --> 00:19:06.074
Didn't she like, sparkle off
into floaty white nothingness


00:19:06.107 --> 00:19:08.143
after Carmilla killed
the giant angler fish god?


00:19:08.176 --> 00:19:10.746
How is that a sentence
I end up saying?


00:19:10.780 --> 00:19:11.614
Only one way to find out.


00:19:13.114 --> 00:19:14.584
We go back to the scene
of the crime.


00:19:14.617 --> 00:19:17.353
If it's ghosts we can test
the new spectrometer...


00:19:20.322 --> 00:19:23.091
- Carm?
- Ooh! Then off-ty off we go!


00:19:23.124 --> 00:19:25.126
Yeah. I'm...


00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:27.597
gonna go crack
another bottle of hemo-soy.


00:19:34.269 --> 00:19:35.671
Hey.


00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:38.741
I'm sorry about the whole
"scene of the crime" thing.


00:19:40.510 --> 00:19:42.545
I know what happened between
you and Elle was complicated.


00:19:42.578 --> 00:19:44.614
- I shouldn't have said that.
- No...


00:19:44.647 --> 00:19:46.516
the scene of the crime
is exactly what it is.


00:19:46.549 --> 00:19:48.451
You saw those dreams.


00:19:48.484 --> 00:19:50.151
You know I...


00:19:51.152 --> 00:19:52.153
...hurt her.


00:19:53.288 --> 00:19:54.357
Hurt you.


00:19:54.390 --> 00:19:56.291
You didn't mean to.


00:19:57.827 --> 00:19:59.662
Maybe there's a silver lining
in all of this.


00:19:59.695 --> 00:20:02.431
If this is Elle trying
to warn us about something,


00:20:02.465 --> 00:20:04.333
maybe you can... help her.


00:20:04.367 --> 00:20:05.668
I'm done being a vampire.


00:20:07.102 --> 00:20:10.138
I'm done dredging up
the past. I'm... done


00:20:10.171 --> 00:20:12.642
with well-meaning
therapists saying,


00:20:12.675 --> 00:20:15.310
"Close your eyes and think
of those you've wronged


00:20:15.344 --> 00:20:17.780
while I light up
this funky incense."


00:20:19.782 --> 00:20:21.817
That's right.


00:20:21.851 --> 00:20:24.687
We have plans, and goals.


00:20:25.821 --> 00:20:27.590
And a colour-coded chart,


00:20:27.623 --> 00:20:30.359
none of which features
some... mystery


00:20:30.393 --> 00:20:33.329
from your past stealing
the life that you earned.


00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:36.131
So we are gonna figure out


00:20:36.164 --> 00:20:38.501
who or what is doing this,
and then we are gonna...


00:20:38.534 --> 00:20:41.169
- Gruesomely murder them...
- Stop them.


00:20:43.606 --> 00:20:45.608
We're goin' back to Styria.


00:20:57.853 --> 00:20:59.789
<i>- Where are we going?
- Styria!</i>


00:20:59.822 --> 00:21:01.724
<i>- Why are we going?
- To stop Carm</i>


00:21:01.757 --> 00:21:03.659
<i>- from re-vamping!
- OK, but really,</i>


00:21:03.693 --> 00:21:05.494
<i>why go to the bad place
with the monsters?</i>


00:21:05.528 --> 00:21:07.330
<i>Because of Elle's
manor. It's in my dreams.</i>


00:21:07.363 --> 00:21:10.333
<i>It's all connected. And it's
our only lead! Ha ha!</i>


00:21:10.366 --> 00:21:12.435
<i>Ooh, schnitzel!</i>


00:21:37.393 --> 00:21:39.428
How much farther
'til we get to this place!?


00:21:40.896 --> 00:21:42.197
It's just...


00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:44.132
Right around the corner.


00:21:50.305 --> 00:21:53.476
Oh, yeah! That's cool, Laura.
I got your bag. Yeah.


00:22:10.291 --> 00:22:11.961
You don't have to do this
if you don't want.


00:22:11.994 --> 00:22:14.229
You can just stay here
if it's too much.


00:22:14.262 --> 00:22:17.298
Hm. And leave you alone


00:22:17.333 --> 00:22:19.300
to explore the mystery mansion?


00:22:19.335 --> 00:22:21.370
Hard pass.


00:22:27.510 --> 00:22:30.311
Hello?


00:23:00.476 --> 00:23:02.812
Hellooo?
Knock knock?


00:23:04.480 --> 00:23:06.281
Elle's manor's pretty cool.


00:23:06.314 --> 00:23:08.350
I guess, if you dig
the Herring Hall vibe.


00:23:09.351 --> 00:23:10.486
Hello?


00:23:11.654 --> 00:23:13.321
Anybody?


00:23:13.355 --> 00:23:14.957
I'm calling it. This place
is totally haunted.


00:23:14.990 --> 00:23:18.427
You don't know that!
Maybe it's just... creaky.


00:23:18.461 --> 00:23:21.330
<i>It's a lovely example
of a 19th-centry schloss.</i>


00:23:21.363 --> 00:23:22.998
<i>Ha. Schloss.</i>


00:23:23.032 --> 00:23:25.801
This is exactly like my dream.
It's beautiful.


00:23:25.835 --> 00:23:27.937
I mean, abandoned and dusty,


00:23:27.970 --> 00:23:29.939
but... beautiful.


00:23:29.972 --> 00:23:32.341
Oh, well, we can
deal with the dust.


00:23:32.374 --> 00:23:33.876
Tell me you did not
bring an entire bag


00:23:33.909 --> 00:23:35.878
- of cleaning supplies.
- Of course I did.


00:23:35.911 --> 00:23:37.413
Do you know what dust
does to expensive equipment?


00:23:39.014 --> 00:23:41.951
We have EMF detectors, Geiger
counters, various spectrometers.


00:23:41.984 --> 00:23:43.819
You didn't think maybe
we'd need some actual weapons?


00:23:43.853 --> 00:23:45.721
Well, knowledge
is really less...


00:23:45.755 --> 00:23:47.723
Pretty sure weapons
are the best weapon.


00:23:47.757 --> 00:23:50.926
Look at this princess.
Carbon-fibre limbs,


00:23:50.960 --> 00:23:52.928
80-pound draw weight,


00:23:52.962 --> 00:23:54.930
capable of shooting
160 feet per second.


00:23:54.964 --> 00:23:56.766
I call her...


00:23:56.799 --> 00:23:57.967
Gertrude.


00:23:58.000 --> 00:24:00.402
- How excessive.
- Excessive?


00:24:00.436 --> 00:24:02.505
Do you remember senior year?


00:24:02.538 --> 00:24:05.407
You were possessed
by Carmilla's mom, the evil god


00:24:05.441 --> 00:24:07.676
who forced the entire student
body - including me - to dig a pit


00:24:07.710 --> 00:24:10.379
to the literal gates of Hell. Or
how about that time Lafontaine


00:24:10.412 --> 00:24:12.848
got brain-sucked by the giant
angler fish monster?


00:24:12.882 --> 00:24:14.850
Or how about the time
that the evil baron


00:24:14.884 --> 00:24:17.386
tried to execute Carmilla?
Or that time that Laura sorta,


00:24:17.419 --> 00:24:19.522
- kinda, I don't know, died?
- We do have


00:24:19.555 --> 00:24:22.391
a lot of back story.


00:24:22.424 --> 00:24:24.827
Fine.


00:24:24.860 --> 00:24:26.796
- Fine. Haunted.
- Tell me at least


00:24:26.829 --> 00:24:28.531
- you two packed some heat?
- Uh, I know Krav Maga.


00:24:28.564 --> 00:24:31.400
I am a weapon.
I brought walkie-talkies


00:24:31.433 --> 00:24:33.402
and flashlights for everyone.


00:24:33.435 --> 00:24:35.070
There's no cell service
out here.


00:24:35.104 --> 00:24:36.539
- They're gonna come in handy.
- How about you, Jughead?


00:24:37.773 --> 00:24:39.742
Oh. Vincent Van Bro
brought beer.


00:24:42.578 --> 00:24:44.747
- Is that her?
- Yeah.


00:24:47.550 --> 00:24:49.718
- Let's search this place!
- For a girl


00:24:49.752 --> 00:24:51.854
who died 150 years ago?


00:24:51.887 --> 00:24:54.456
Better not keep her waiting.


00:25:52.748 --> 00:25:55.417
- Is that you?
- It was.


00:26:06.462 --> 00:26:08.797
We should be safe to push the meeting
to next week, don't you think?


00:26:08.831 --> 00:26:10.499
Do we have to talk
about this right now?


00:26:10.532 --> 00:26:12.134
The single most important
meeting of our careers?


00:26:12.167 --> 00:26:14.136
Per, we are searching
a haunted castle for ghosts.


00:26:14.169 --> 00:26:16.639
This is literally the reason
we started the company.


00:26:16.672 --> 00:26:18.641
- But if we had more resources...
- Hold on, I think I got a hit.


00:26:18.674 --> 00:26:20.442
No, it's gone now.


00:26:20.476 --> 00:26:22.511
Well, now, see, as part
of Intrigue, we'd have all


00:26:22.544 --> 00:26:24.513
the equipment, we could scan
the house in like, two seconds!


00:26:24.546 --> 00:26:27.049
Yeah. I get it, but we're not
selling out right this second.


00:26:27.082 --> 00:26:28.817
So can we focus
on the task at hand?


00:26:29.985 --> 00:26:31.754
Let's check out
the next room.


00:26:50.039 --> 00:26:52.074
Looking forward to seeing her?


00:26:52.107 --> 00:26:53.943
Elle, I mean?


00:26:53.976 --> 00:26:56.011
I wouldn't blame you
if you were.


00:26:57.012 --> 00:26:58.847
Honestly, I'd rather not.


00:26:59.848 --> 00:27:02.117
What am I supposed to say?


00:27:02.151 --> 00:27:03.953
Sorry I lied to you
and sacrificed you


00:27:03.986 --> 00:27:05.921
to a giant fish monster?


00:27:05.955 --> 00:27:08.490
I doubt there's a Hallmark card.


00:27:09.291 --> 00:27:11.527
It wasn't all your fault.


00:27:30.045 --> 00:27:32.014
I told her these
were gonna come in handy!


00:27:32.047 --> 00:27:34.249
<i>Ghosts! The schloss
is full of ghosts!</i>


00:27:37.319 --> 00:27:39.755
GHOST! Ghost!


00:27:39.788 --> 00:27:41.757
- Everyone, come on! Come on!
- Haunted house!


00:27:41.790 --> 00:27:44.093
- Totally called it!
- Where do we go?!


00:27:44.126 --> 00:27:46.095
- Go!
- Holy crap! Oh, crap!


00:27:46.128 --> 00:27:49.098
- Go, go! - Perry, do something!
- Go, go, go, go!


00:27:49.131 --> 00:27:51.867
- God, it's stuck!
- Come on!


00:27:53.936 --> 00:27:56.638
Ghosts! Ghosts!
Guys! Guys!


00:27:58.741 --> 00:28:01.610
- Let me out!
- Oh! Oh!


00:28:01.643 --> 00:28:03.545
- Ooh!
- Uh, guys...


00:28:10.786 --> 00:28:12.755
Um...


00:28:12.788 --> 00:28:14.323
Hi.


00:28:14.357 --> 00:28:16.625
I'm Laura. These
are my friends...


00:28:16.658 --> 00:28:18.093
and we'd be thrilled


00:28:18.127 --> 00:28:20.229
if you'd abandon your plans
to gruesomely murder us.


00:28:20.262 --> 00:28:23.265
Hello, Miss Karnstein.


00:28:24.833 --> 00:28:25.834
Hello...


00:28:29.271 --> 00:28:30.272
Wait. I know you.


00:28:31.673 --> 00:28:32.875
How do I know you?


00:28:33.976 --> 00:28:35.811
Oh, dear.
Well, this is awkward.


00:28:37.312 --> 00:28:38.947
We imagined you'd recall...


00:28:38.981 --> 00:28:41.283
Killing us.


00:28:41.316 --> 00:28:43.852
I'm Charlotte.
This is my sister, Emily.


00:28:43.886 --> 00:28:48.190
- Carmilla killed you?
- Oh... no, not quite, exactly.


00:28:48.223 --> 00:28:50.893
Her mother did
the actual deed.


00:28:50.926 --> 00:28:52.861
You're the girls


00:28:52.895 --> 00:28:54.863
who were sacrificed
to the Deep One.


00:28:57.733 --> 00:28:58.700
Yes.


00:28:58.734 --> 00:29:01.036
We are the victims


00:29:01.070 --> 00:29:03.038
of Carmilla Karnstein...


00:29:07.643 --> 00:29:10.145
...and we'd like
to invite you to dinner.


00:29:13.816 --> 00:29:16.185
It's wonderful that you've
all been able to join us.


00:29:17.853 --> 00:29:21.391
And naturally, we're so glad
you've arrived in time.


00:29:21.424 --> 00:29:24.159
We've been waiting for weeks.


00:29:24.193 --> 00:29:26.662
- For us?
- For Miss Karnstein.


00:29:26.695 --> 00:29:29.298
We hoped once she realized
what had happened, she'd return.


00:29:29.332 --> 00:29:31.967
Hold up. Did you just confess


00:29:32.000 --> 00:29:34.636
to flipping the vampire switch
on our girl Carm here?


00:29:34.670 --> 00:29:36.805
Oh. Goodness, no.
We couldn't have.


00:29:36.839 --> 00:29:38.341
What little research


00:29:38.374 --> 00:29:41.344
we have been able to perform
suggests it was Miss Karnstein's


00:29:41.377 --> 00:29:44.046
<i>life force that pulled us
into the physical world.</i>


00:29:45.047 --> 00:29:47.082
Until a few weeks ago,


00:29:47.116 --> 00:29:49.685
we were trapped in a
nightmare land, doomed


00:29:49.718 --> 00:29:51.687
to endlessly repeat
our greatest regret.


00:29:51.720 --> 00:29:54.756
This nightmare afterlife, is
it more of a Jungian-unconscious


00:29:54.790 --> 00:29:57.126
or a through-the-looking-glass-
to-hell situation?


00:29:57.159 --> 00:29:58.361
Stop that!


00:29:58.394 --> 00:30:00.195
It's not polite to pry
into other people's


00:30:00.229 --> 00:30:02.731
- unspeakable suffering.
- Why would you be connected


00:30:02.764 --> 00:30:04.733
- to Carmilla's human life?
- Ah.


00:30:05.901 --> 00:30:09.138
We think it might be
because it was


00:30:09.171 --> 00:30:11.974
- Miss Karnstein who...
- She's the reason we died.


00:30:13.909 --> 00:30:15.711
Yes.


00:30:15.744 --> 00:30:18.780
The family here offered my
sister and I a place to lodge.


00:30:18.814 --> 00:30:20.782
They neglected to mention
the vampire cult.


00:30:20.816 --> 00:30:23.353
Same thing happened with
my college acceptance letter.


00:30:23.386 --> 00:30:25.988
You said you knew the family.
Does that mean


00:30:26.021 --> 00:30:27.723
that you knew Elle?


00:30:29.392 --> 00:30:30.726
Miss Sheridan.


00:30:30.759 --> 00:30:33.061
Ah. Yes. We knew her.


00:30:35.063 --> 00:30:37.966
- But she isn't here with you?
- No.


00:30:38.967 --> 00:30:40.235
She isn't with us.


00:30:42.104 --> 00:30:44.072
But...


00:30:44.106 --> 00:30:46.275
we're thrilled that you are!


00:30:46.308 --> 00:30:48.277
OK. That's it.


00:30:49.445 --> 00:30:50.846
What's with the Stepford act?


00:30:51.947 --> 00:30:53.483
I got you and
your sister killed.


00:30:53.516 --> 00:30:55.751
Yes, but you're here now.


00:30:55.784 --> 00:30:57.453
And according to
this spell book,


00:30:57.487 --> 00:30:59.922
we need you,
Carmilla, here


00:30:59.955 --> 00:31:02.724
to perform the ritual
that will let us move on.


00:31:04.394 --> 00:31:06.795
I don't suppose
I could take a crack


00:31:06.828 --> 00:31:08.263
- at deciphering the book?
- Oh!


00:31:08.297 --> 00:31:11.200
Please, do. I've
deciphered what I can,


00:31:11.233 --> 00:31:13.369
but I'm hardly
an adept. Ah...


00:31:13.403 --> 00:31:15.938
From what I can tell,
if we move on,


00:31:15.971 --> 00:31:18.941
your vampire symptoms
will go away.


00:31:18.974 --> 00:31:21.176
I assume that's why
you've come?


00:31:22.345 --> 00:31:23.745
Haven't you?


00:31:26.848 --> 00:31:28.917
Because otherwise, you'd be
trapped here with us forever.


00:31:30.786 --> 00:31:32.455
<i>So, they're obviously evil.</i>


00:31:32.488 --> 00:31:34.289
I thought they
were kind of nice!


00:31:35.290 --> 00:31:36.825
More importantly,


00:31:36.858 --> 00:31:38.894
is this ritual of theirs
even gonna fix me?


00:31:38.927 --> 00:31:40.963
- It looks promising.
- Promising?


00:31:40.996 --> 00:31:44.099
Are you telling me you were
possessed by an evil goddess


00:31:44.132 --> 00:31:46.868
- for like six months and...
- Eight. It was eight months.


00:31:48.504 --> 00:31:50.305
...and you can't get
more specific than that?


00:31:50.340 --> 00:31:53.308
The whole book
is written in code,


00:31:53.343 --> 00:31:55.210
but... if Emily's
notes are correct,


00:31:55.244 --> 00:31:57.513
it seems as though
it's two birds, one stone.


00:31:57.547 --> 00:32:00.483
The ghosts move on,
Carmilla stays human.


00:32:00.516 --> 00:32:02.951
That makes sense. When I
scanned them, the energy


00:32:02.985 --> 00:32:04.886
from your spark was
going straight to them.


00:32:04.920 --> 00:32:07.222
For all we know, they lured us
in and trapped us here. Are we


00:32:07.256 --> 00:32:08.558
- seriously gonna trust them?
- What happened to them


00:32:08.591 --> 00:32:10.792
wasn't their fault.
They were girls,


00:32:10.826 --> 00:32:12.894
just like you or me, with
their whole lives ahead of them.


00:32:12.928 --> 00:32:14.997
If this ritual helps them
and keeps Carm human,


00:32:15.030 --> 00:32:17.099
we have to try it.


00:32:30.078 --> 00:32:32.515
- Sweet! Is that a Gameboy?
- Even better.


00:32:32.548 --> 00:32:34.384
It's an EMF alarm.
Might be nice


00:32:34.417 --> 00:32:36.151
to get a heads up
if any ghosts come calling.


00:32:44.226 --> 00:32:46.362
Listen, Per, about before...


00:32:46.396 --> 00:32:48.431
Oh, I'm glad we postponed
the meeting.


00:32:48.464 --> 00:32:50.433
- You are?
- With all the data


00:32:50.466 --> 00:32:51.900
we've collected here,


00:32:51.933 --> 00:32:53.235
we're in a much stronger
bargaining position.


00:32:54.870 --> 00:32:55.937
Really, Per?


00:32:56.938 --> 00:32:58.374
I know this is the big leagues,


00:32:58.408 --> 00:33:00.510
<i>but why are you so pumped
to sell our company?</i>


00:33:02.010 --> 00:33:03.379
Do you even know
what I do all day


00:33:03.413 --> 00:33:05.381
while you're off playing
in your little lab?


00:33:05.415 --> 00:33:08.917
I balance our budgets,
get our products approved,


00:33:08.950 --> 00:33:10.386
handle the reckless endangerment
lawsuits.


00:33:10.420 --> 00:33:11.920
I mean, at Intrigue,
there'd be a...


00:33:11.953 --> 00:33:13.389
Ahem.


00:33:13.423 --> 00:33:16.392
There'd be
a legal department, Laf.


00:33:16.426 --> 00:33:18.060
I see.


00:33:18.093 --> 00:33:19.529
And, uh, by playing,


00:33:19.562 --> 00:33:21.263
you mean the research
that makes our company possible?


00:33:21.296 --> 00:33:23.098
- Oh, that is not fair and...
- You know what?


00:33:23.131 --> 00:33:25.233
I'm too tired to deal
with this right now.


00:33:37.112 --> 00:33:39.281
Oh, man! We killed
my sandwich.


00:33:41.617 --> 00:33:43.586
Too tee abal too tee!


00:33:43.619 --> 00:33:45.655
Five second rule.


00:33:45.688 --> 00:33:48.890
Have we or have we not
had multiple conversations


00:33:48.924 --> 00:33:51.361
about not wandering away
in the haunted house?


00:33:51.394 --> 00:33:53.261
I know. It's just,
the ghost ladies are so nice.


00:33:53.295 --> 00:33:54.530
And you know how I feel
about leftovers.


00:33:54.564 --> 00:33:57.032
Kirsch, if your stomach
gets me dragged


00:33:57.065 --> 00:33:59.369
into some kind of black-girl-
dies-first bullshit...


00:33:59.402 --> 00:34:02.871
I am going to come back from the
dead and haunt your bar fridge.


00:34:11.347 --> 00:34:13.014
They aren't going
to go along with it.


00:34:13.048 --> 00:34:16.118
They'll get caught up
in the surprise! You'll see.


00:34:16.151 --> 00:34:18.120
It will all come out
exactly as we planned.


00:34:18.153 --> 00:34:20.456
Why aren't we just telling them about...


00:34:58.461 --> 00:35:01.330
Ugh. This again? Really?


00:35:04.400 --> 00:35:06.301
You would do well,
little sister, to finish...


00:35:08.571 --> 00:35:11.474
<i>We live for the eternal
moment, chérie.</i>


00:35:11.507 --> 00:35:13.275
We are power.


00:35:18.714 --> 00:35:21.049
<i>Faites attention, chérie.</i>


00:35:21.082 --> 00:35:22.518
You would do well,
little sister,


00:35:22.552 --> 00:35:24.720
to finish your task here
without further delay.


00:35:24.754 --> 00:35:27.557
Did you ever think
that our part in this...


00:35:28.558 --> 00:35:30.225
...that what we do might be...


00:35:31.226 --> 00:35:32.495
...unforgivable?


00:35:32.528 --> 00:35:34.963
You must stop reading
the romantics!


00:35:36.231 --> 00:35:38.701
<i>We live for the eternal
moment, chérie!</i>


00:35:38.734 --> 00:35:41.704
We are power, pleasure...


00:35:43.539 --> 00:35:46.208
...and are only accountable
for our desires.


00:35:46.241 --> 00:35:48.411
And Mama, who
is growing impatient.


00:35:48.444 --> 00:35:51.714
<i>Faites attention, chérie.
Votre mère vous met en garde</i>


00:35:51.747 --> 00:35:53.583
<i>contre l'assassin.</i>


00:36:12.502 --> 00:36:15.404
<i>You're wearing
the brooch.</i>


00:36:24.647 --> 00:36:26.716
<i>No!
I don't want to go back!</i>


00:36:27.683 --> 00:36:30.185
Hey...


00:36:32.120 --> 00:36:33.154
You all right?


00:36:34.624 --> 00:36:36.459
Another nightmare.


00:36:37.627 --> 00:36:40.095
You and Maddie
were talking, and...


00:36:40.128 --> 00:36:42.097
she said something
about an assassin


00:36:42.130 --> 00:36:44.467
and then these paper dolls
disintegrated and...


00:36:46.301 --> 00:36:49.438
I don't know. It seemed more
coherent when it was happening.


00:36:49.472 --> 00:36:51.807
Wait, you're still
having those dreams?


00:36:51.841 --> 00:36:53.809
But we're here. I mean...


00:36:55.310 --> 00:36:57.680
Why would you still
be having them, unless...


00:36:57.713 --> 00:36:59.715
Something else is going on.


00:36:59.749 --> 00:37:02.685
Knocking. Still not a thing.


00:37:02.718 --> 00:37:04.520
The Hunger wanted a midnight
snack and while he was


00:37:04.554 --> 00:37:06.556
getting it, we caught
our ghostesses talking


00:37:06.589 --> 00:37:08.858
about some kind of surprise
that we aren't gonna like


00:37:08.891 --> 00:37:11.326
and sneaking into a locked room.
So, they're hiding


00:37:11.360 --> 00:37:13.763
something. Or someone.


00:37:15.331 --> 00:37:18.166
Hiding something?!
How could we possibly...


00:37:18.199 --> 00:37:20.469
- What's behind the door?
- Why should that concern you?


00:37:20.503 --> 00:37:22.405
Maybe I don't like surprises.


00:37:22.438 --> 00:37:24.139
You look like a woman
who can cope.


00:37:24.172 --> 00:37:25.775
This could all be


00:37:25.808 --> 00:37:27.777
easily resolved by just
showing us what's behind


00:37:27.810 --> 00:37:30.111
- door number one.
- Of course.


00:37:30.145 --> 00:37:32.515
If you insist, but...


00:37:32.548 --> 00:37:34.750
you'll ruin the surprise.


00:37:34.784 --> 00:37:37.353
We'll risk it.


00:37:40.623 --> 00:37:43.291
We'd kinda like to know
if you're planning to...


00:37:45.861 --> 00:37:47.262
...to throw a party?


00:37:48.864 --> 00:37:52.602
- To thank you for helping us.
- You're throwing a party?


00:37:52.635 --> 00:37:55.671
The ritual can't be performed
until the Ash Moon begins,


00:37:55.705 --> 00:37:56.706
and Emily always
loved to dress up.


00:37:58.708 --> 00:38:01.410
I can't imagine you're a slouch
in that department either.


00:38:01.444 --> 00:38:04.413
- You can't be serious.
- I think it's sweet!


00:38:04.447 --> 00:38:06.782
It's like a pre-ritual,
going away party...


00:38:06.816 --> 00:38:08.551
before they go away.


00:38:09.719 --> 00:38:12.722
- Permanently.
- Exactly, and...


00:38:14.255 --> 00:38:15.858
...we would be honoured
if you would attend.


00:38:15.891 --> 00:38:17.693
Yeah, of course!


00:38:17.727 --> 00:38:19.328
Oh, my gosh.


00:38:22.398 --> 00:38:25.735
<i>Ball gowns? Are we gonna
get our Strictly Ballroom on?!</i>


00:38:25.768 --> 00:38:28.571
Best haunting ever!


00:38:34.644 --> 00:38:36.646
<i>How's it
goin' in there?</i>


00:38:36.679 --> 00:38:39.815
BBC period dramas
do not spend enough time on


00:38:39.849 --> 00:38:41.717
how complicated
these clothes are.


00:38:41.751 --> 00:38:43.786
I swear I've been in here
for 40 minutes.


00:38:43.819 --> 00:38:47.188
Hey, thanks for going along
with this, by the way.


00:38:47.222 --> 00:38:50.225
Well, what's to go along with?
I like canapes


00:38:50.258 --> 00:38:51.894
- as much as the next girl.
- Still...


00:38:51.927 --> 00:38:53.729
can't be fun
hanging out with your...


00:38:53.763 --> 00:38:57.500
- Former victims?
- No matter how nice they are.


00:38:57.533 --> 00:38:59.935
Yeah, well, I'd appreciate it
if they took it down a notch.


00:38:59.969 --> 00:39:01.904
You'd prefer a roaring rampage
of revenge?


00:39:01.937 --> 00:39:04.407
Yeah. All this forgiveness
is making me twitchy.


00:39:05.841 --> 00:39:07.576
Do you think maybe
that's 'cause, deep down,


00:39:07.610 --> 00:39:08.811
you still don't think
you can be forgiven?


00:39:10.946 --> 00:39:15.351
I see we've reached the
amateur psychoanalysis round.


00:39:15.384 --> 00:39:18.286
See, this is why I
blew off that therapist.


00:39:18.319 --> 00:39:20.756
You know, some things are just


00:39:20.790 --> 00:39:23.626
too much to talk about in an
office full of crystal dolphins.


00:39:23.659 --> 00:39:25.895
Do you think maybe that's
the point of the talking?


00:39:25.928 --> 00:39:27.763
Yeah, except it
wasn't just talking.


00:39:27.797 --> 00:39:30.265
There was this manifes...


00:39:32.835 --> 00:39:34.670
You aren't saying anything.


00:39:37.573 --> 00:39:39.709
Did I put it on wrong?
I look ridiculous.


00:39:39.742 --> 00:39:41.242
I do. I look ridiculous. I...


00:40:04.299 --> 00:40:06.502
40 minutes to get you
into that, huh?


00:40:08.504 --> 00:40:10.840
Bet I could get you
out of it faster....


00:40:21.851 --> 00:40:23.686
We're already gonna
be late for the ball.


00:40:24.854 --> 00:40:26.722
So let us be late.


00:41:51.574 --> 00:41:53.576
♪ Love


00:42:50.165 --> 00:42:51.834
I'm coming.


00:43:18.560 --> 00:43:20.796
Looking good, bruv!


00:43:23.699 --> 00:43:26.201
- What?
- May I have this dance?


00:43:28.237 --> 00:43:30.472
Come on.


00:43:36.512 --> 00:43:37.880
Sorry about the way
I handled things last night.


00:43:37.913 --> 00:43:38.847
That's all right. I know
you didn't mean any of it.


00:43:40.716 --> 00:43:42.952
I may have been a bit harsh,
that doesn't mean I was wrong.


00:43:42.985 --> 00:43:44.820
Let's not fight in front
of the ghosts, honey.


00:43:53.929 --> 00:43:55.230
It's not your thing
either, huh?


00:43:58.867 --> 00:44:02.204
Emily has always
wanted to belong to society.


00:44:02.237 --> 00:44:04.473
I understood
life differently.


00:44:06.275 --> 00:44:08.577
If you have to conform,
you never belonged.


00:44:10.579 --> 00:44:13.082
OK. How did you fall
for Vampirella's schtick?


00:44:14.083 --> 00:44:15.751
I didn't.


00:44:15.784 --> 00:44:18.087
My sister vanished.


00:44:19.088 --> 00:44:20.089
I went looking for her.


00:44:22.624 --> 00:44:24.593
She's never
forgiven herself.


00:44:24.626 --> 00:44:26.261
What about you?


00:44:26.295 --> 00:44:28.764
I didn't leave her then...


00:44:30.632 --> 00:44:31.834
How could I now?


00:44:33.769 --> 00:44:36.071
You wanna try
this stupid dance?


00:44:38.073 --> 00:44:39.842
Obviously.


00:45:03.799 --> 00:45:05.000
This is nice.


00:45:06.135 --> 00:45:07.770
Kinda like that grad ball
we never got


00:45:07.803 --> 00:45:09.772
'cause our school
was a supernatural death trap.


00:45:13.675 --> 00:45:15.210
I missed this.


00:45:16.678 --> 00:45:18.614
I mean, not the pulse-pounding
terror, but...


00:45:18.647 --> 00:45:20.616
the parts where we help people.


00:45:21.683 --> 00:45:22.918
Though I do wish we'd figure out


00:45:22.951 --> 00:45:24.920
why the ghosts were here
in the first place.


00:45:26.155 --> 00:45:28.957
- Hey, Laura...
- I know.


00:45:28.991 --> 00:45:30.926
No need to keep prying.


00:45:30.959 --> 00:45:32.828
The ghosts will move on.


00:45:32.861 --> 00:45:34.296
You will get your life back


00:45:34.330 --> 00:45:36.332
and... we can go back home.


00:45:38.167 --> 00:45:40.669
No. I, um... I think


00:45:40.702 --> 00:45:43.739
at that therapist's appointment,
I may have, um...


00:45:50.145 --> 00:45:52.047
Laura?


00:45:54.716 --> 00:45:56.718
Sorry.


00:45:58.687 --> 00:46:00.756
Weird déjà vu.


00:46:07.963 --> 00:46:09.865
Hey.


00:46:11.033 --> 00:46:12.067
- What's going on?
- I thought...


00:46:13.369 --> 00:46:15.170
I thought I saw the woman
in black, the...


00:46:15.204 --> 00:46:17.340
You.


00:46:17.373 --> 00:46:19.741
The you from
my dreams, but...


00:46:22.878 --> 00:46:24.213
That's impossible, right?


00:46:26.748 --> 00:46:28.750
Come on. Let's sit down.


00:46:36.758 --> 00:46:38.060
I'll get you
a drink, OK?


00:46:45.100 --> 00:46:48.036
Come with me
lovingly to death,


00:46:48.070 --> 00:46:50.373
or else hate me
and still come with me,


00:46:50.406 --> 00:46:52.408
hating me through death


00:46:52.442 --> 00:46:53.976
and after.


00:46:58.113 --> 00:46:59.415
Are you OK?


00:47:09.925 --> 00:47:11.126
Where is she?!


00:47:11.160 --> 00:47:13.429
- Hey...
- She was right here.


00:47:13.463 --> 00:47:15.264
- What's going on, Hollis?
- The woman in black!


00:47:15.297 --> 00:47:16.999
- The one wearing a mask!
- Everybody's wearing a mask.


00:47:18.200 --> 00:47:20.202
Do you know
who she's talking about?


00:47:21.937 --> 00:47:24.273
Maybe if you're not feeling
well, you should sit down.


00:47:24.306 --> 00:47:26.808
I'm dreaming things
while I'm awake now.


00:47:26.842 --> 00:47:28.777
What's next?


00:47:35.184 --> 00:47:37.286
It's almost time!


00:47:37.319 --> 00:47:40.122
The Ash Moon has begun.


00:47:40.155 --> 00:47:42.257
Gather round for the ritual.


00:47:42.291 --> 00:47:45.194
Before we begin, I want to say


00:47:45.227 --> 00:47:47.829
how grateful we are.


00:47:47.863 --> 00:47:49.465
Whatever you've done
in the past,


00:47:49.499 --> 00:47:52.000
you've come to help us now,


00:47:52.034 --> 00:47:55.137
and I think that shows
a strength of character


00:47:55.170 --> 00:47:57.239
that is quite remarkable.


00:47:59.174 --> 00:48:01.810
Yeah. Sure.


00:48:03.312 --> 00:48:04.846
It's time, Emily.


00:48:07.115 --> 00:48:08.951
It's your last night on Earth.


00:48:08.984 --> 00:48:11.421
Are you sure you don't want
another drink before you go?


00:48:11.454 --> 00:48:14.457
The ritual must be performed
before the Ash Moon


00:48:14.490 --> 00:48:17.527
ends at sunrise. Otherwise,
we're trapped here forever.


00:48:17.560 --> 00:48:20.330
So... no.


00:48:31.574 --> 00:48:33.543
Wait, that's
the brooch that I...


00:48:37.045 --> 00:48:38.514
Carm?


00:48:41.351 --> 00:48:43.051
That's Carmilla's spark!


00:48:45.355 --> 00:48:47.357
It's leaving her! Why...
why is it going into the brooch?


00:48:50.926 --> 00:48:52.794
- Uh... guys?
- Did that spell


00:48:52.828 --> 00:48:54.430
say anything
about spirit entanglement?


00:48:54.464 --> 00:48:55.964
It's not supposed
to happen like this!


00:48:55.998 --> 00:48:58.000
- Something's wrong.
- Laura, stay back!


00:48:58.033 --> 00:48:59.502
- It's dangerous!
- We have to stop the ritual!


00:48:59.535 --> 00:49:01.103
I can't!


00:49:01.136 --> 00:49:03.805
- It's out of control!
- Emily, no!


00:49:03.839 --> 00:49:07.175
We've been tricked!
I don't want to go back!


00:49:07.209 --> 00:49:09.845
We need to disrupt
the connection!


00:49:09.878 --> 00:49:12.014
- LAF!
- Don't touch Carmilla!


00:49:12.047 --> 00:49:13.048
It'll take you too!


00:49:26.396 --> 00:49:29.164
Did you think you'd
get away with it?


00:49:31.601 --> 00:49:34.236
Summon us up to ease
your mind and then...


00:49:34.269 --> 00:49:36.238
just waltz away?


00:49:36.271 --> 00:49:39.074
Did you really think
there'd be no consequences?


00:49:43.646 --> 00:49:45.615
It's you.


00:49:45.648 --> 00:49:47.949
Surprise!


00:49:49.585 --> 00:49:51.521
Not the brightest
little ingénue, are we?


00:50:19.382 --> 00:50:21.417
Is that pile
of dust Lafontaine?!


00:50:21.451 --> 00:50:24.052
They're j... they're
just g... gone.


00:50:24.086 --> 00:50:26.589
- Are you OK?
- Carm?


00:50:26.622 --> 00:50:28.524
- I need to hide.
- Carm?


00:50:28.558 --> 00:50:30.526
Carm?!


00:50:36.632 --> 00:50:38.668
Carm!


00:50:38.701 --> 00:50:40.636
Carm!


00:50:40.670 --> 00:50:42.538
Hey!


00:50:42.572 --> 00:50:45.307
Hey! Come on! Hey!


00:50:45.341 --> 00:50:47.943
Carm! Hey! Hey!


00:50:47.976 --> 00:50:50.546
Hey! Hey!


00:50:50.580 --> 00:50:53.516
Hey...


00:51:12.100 --> 00:51:13.603
Your heart.
It's not beating.


00:51:16.506 --> 00:51:18.240
You're a vampire.


00:51:18.273 --> 00:51:20.942
<i>NOOO!</i>


00:51:20.976 --> 00:51:23.479
Why won't it work?!
I've sent all the ghosts away!


00:51:32.988 --> 00:51:34.956
Did one of them escape me?


00:51:39.060 --> 00:51:40.663
So did I miss something,
or did that radically


00:51:40.696 --> 00:51:42.532
- not go as planned?
- It was Elle.


00:51:42.565 --> 00:51:44.567
She was at the masquerade. She
knew about the ritual. She knew


00:51:44.600 --> 00:51:47.135
- exactly what was gonna happen.
- How could she have known?


00:51:47.169 --> 00:51:48.970
Because Emily
and Charlotte lied to us.


00:51:49.004 --> 00:51:50.606
They had to have
known she was here.


00:51:50.640 --> 00:51:53.376
You think vacuumed, screaming
back to a hellish nightmarescape


00:51:53.409 --> 00:51:54.710
was part of their plan?


00:51:55.711 --> 00:51:58.347
Sorry.


00:51:58.381 --> 00:52:01.183
We will figure this out.
We will find Laf.


00:52:01.216 --> 00:52:03.519
Why would Elle do this?


00:52:03.553 --> 00:52:05.354
You heard her...


00:52:05.388 --> 00:52:08.056
to punish me for what I did
by stealing my life.


00:52:08.089 --> 00:52:10.258
But she can't steal anything.
She's trapped here,


00:52:10.292 --> 00:52:12.260
just like us, unless
all the ghosts move on.


00:52:12.294 --> 00:52:14.430
But the ghosts are gone.
All of them


00:52:14.464 --> 00:52:17.065
except Elle and Charlotte.
Elle can't leave until Charlotte


00:52:17.098 --> 00:52:19.000
is also sent back
to the nightmare land,


00:52:19.034 --> 00:52:21.136
like all the other ghosts.
Laf thwarted her plan.


00:52:21.169 --> 00:52:23.539
And now that my spark's
in the brooch


00:52:23.573 --> 00:52:26.542
and Elle has the brooch, if she
gets rid of Charlotte...


00:52:26.576 --> 00:52:29.010
she could become human
and leave.


00:52:32.648 --> 00:52:35.384
We have to find her. Now.


00:52:35.418 --> 00:52:37.386
That's easier said than done.


00:52:37.420 --> 00:52:39.221
Miss Sheridan is gone, girl.


00:52:39.254 --> 00:52:41.089
Yeah. Not to mention,
we don't exactly know


00:52:41.122 --> 00:52:43.459
how to extract a life force
from a magical brooch.


00:52:43.493 --> 00:52:46.362
Might wanna go easy on those.
That's the only case.


00:52:47.363 --> 00:52:48.129
Terrific.


00:52:49.365 --> 00:52:51.233
But... Elle must have
the spell already.


00:52:51.266 --> 00:52:53.402
I mean, that's
her escape plan, right?


00:52:53.436 --> 00:52:55.270
So we have to find Elle
before she gets to Charlotte;


00:52:55.303 --> 00:52:57.740
- then Perry can find the spell...
- What are you talking about?


00:52:57.773 --> 00:53:00.242
- We have to find Laf first.
- Of course, we have to find


00:53:00.275 --> 00:53:02.545
both of them, but if we lose Elle now,
then all of us are gonna be trapped...


00:53:02.578 --> 00:53:04.547
We can find Elle later.
Laf comes first!


00:53:04.580 --> 00:53:06.649
We can't just let her
take Carmilla's life!


00:53:14.524 --> 00:53:16.459
We could start
in the study.


00:53:16.492 --> 00:53:18.427
I can't believe I'm saying
this, but beef cheeks is right.


00:53:18.461 --> 00:53:21.263
We don't have much time.


00:53:25.300 --> 00:53:27.269
I need to get out
of this dress.


00:53:27.302 --> 00:53:29.271
- It'll be easier if you...
- Did you summon up the ghosts?


00:53:29.304 --> 00:53:32.240
Because that's what she said,
Elle, that you summoned her up.


00:53:32.274 --> 00:53:35.378
- I think it's possible.
- Possible?


00:53:35.411 --> 00:53:38.146
How do you not know whether
you summoned up the ghosts


00:53:38.179 --> 00:53:39.815
of your former victims who want
some light, refreshing revenge?


00:53:39.849 --> 00:53:41.817
Because it was
just something stupid


00:53:41.851 --> 00:53:43.519
that happened at
the therapist appointment.


00:53:44.520 --> 00:53:47.155
- What?
- She... said


00:53:47.188 --> 00:53:49.090
I could never move forward
unless I dealt


00:53:49.124 --> 00:53:52.093
with my past. So...
she had me think about Elle


00:53:52.127 --> 00:53:54.463
and the others and, you know,
there was the usual


00:53:54.497 --> 00:53:58.568
"manifest your issues" crap
but... I had forgotten


00:53:58.601 --> 00:54:00.536
all about it until my issues


00:54:00.570 --> 00:54:02.605
actually... manifested.


00:54:02.638 --> 00:54:04.874
When were you gonna share this
piece of information with me?


00:54:04.907 --> 00:54:06.542
I was waiting
for the right moment.


00:54:06.576 --> 00:54:08.377
You know what
would've been a good moment?


00:54:08.411 --> 00:54:11.313
Any time before the ghost
of your former lover killed you.


00:54:14.350 --> 00:54:15.718
She killed you.


00:54:17.920 --> 00:54:19.655
I thought she killed you.


00:54:19.689 --> 00:54:22.491
Hey... come here.


00:54:24.493 --> 00:54:26.495
I'm still here.


00:54:26.529 --> 00:54:28.564
OK? I'm still here.


00:54:30.433 --> 00:54:33.469
We're gonna get
my life back. OK?


00:54:33.502 --> 00:54:35.605
And all those things we want,


00:54:35.638 --> 00:54:37.907
every single point


00:54:37.940 --> 00:54:41.344
on your five-year-plan,
we're gonna do them, OK?


00:54:43.346 --> 00:54:47.148
OK. Come on, let's
get you out of this thing.


00:54:48.718 --> 00:54:49.819
<i>Either Emily decoded</i>


00:54:49.852 --> 00:54:52.421
the spell wrong,
or Elle tricked her.


00:54:52.455 --> 00:54:55.391
The spell she did cast used
Carmilla's spark to force the ghosts


00:54:55.424 --> 00:54:57.192
off to the nightmare land
that Emily described.


00:54:58.561 --> 00:55:00.529
You think that's where
the Brainiac ended up?


00:55:03.298 --> 00:55:05.166
Do you think you
can get them back?


00:55:05.200 --> 00:55:07.168
I think the real moving on
spell might do it.


00:55:07.202 --> 00:55:09.772
But... that means we
only have 'til sunrise


00:55:09.805 --> 00:55:13.743
to find the code key.
And I'll need Carmilla's spark.


00:55:13.776 --> 00:55:16.177
Well, that makes getting
the brooch back priority one.


00:55:16.211 --> 00:55:17.513
Hollis'll be chiffed.


00:55:19.415 --> 00:55:20.416
Perry...


00:55:21.817 --> 00:55:23.786
Lafontaine knows
you're looking for them.


00:55:23.819 --> 00:55:26.555
They know.


00:55:26.589 --> 00:55:28.524
It's what we do.


00:55:43.304 --> 00:55:46.274
It's done. We leave tonight.


00:55:46.307 --> 00:55:49.445
In 3 days, we'll be on an ocean
liner headed for New York.


00:55:58.954 --> 00:56:01.424
You're gonna love New York.


00:56:01.457 --> 00:56:03.224
It's full of... concerts


00:56:03.258 --> 00:56:05.226
and theatre


00:56:05.260 --> 00:56:07.396
and... life.


00:56:07.430 --> 00:56:09.532
Your life is gonna be


00:56:09.565 --> 00:56:12.233
so much bigger
than you ever imagined!


00:56:16.038 --> 00:56:19.575
What are you doing?


00:56:31.387 --> 00:56:32.822
Laura!


00:56:33.823 --> 00:56:35.825
Hey... are you all right?


00:56:39.595 --> 00:56:41.897
What in Stoker's name
is going on?


00:56:44.533 --> 00:56:47.302
So Elle can dream-kebab
you in real life?


00:56:47.336 --> 00:56:49.270
Is that a normal ghost thing?
Were we supposed to know


00:56:49.304 --> 00:56:51.306
- they could do that?
- She sent me dreams before.


00:56:51.340 --> 00:56:53.375
This is the first time she's
reached out and slashed me.


00:56:53.409 --> 00:56:55.444
- Oh, dear.
- No, no, no, no, no.


00:56:55.478 --> 00:56:57.780
Not "Oh, dear." We do not
need an "Oh, dear" right now.


00:56:57.813 --> 00:57:00.416
Well, I'm still deciphering
but there are several spells


00:57:00.449 --> 00:57:02.985
in this book which might make
the ghosts much more powerful,


00:57:03.018 --> 00:57:05.588
- especially in the dream world.
- Right.


00:57:05.621 --> 00:57:08.289
So Elle's better,
faster, stronger.


00:57:08.323 --> 00:57:10.025
Can we undo that?


00:57:10.059 --> 00:57:11.994
Use the book
to soup ourselves up?


00:57:12.027 --> 00:57:15.631
"Side effects may include
anxiety, insomnia,


00:57:15.664 --> 00:57:17.967
dream contagion
and... death."


00:57:18.000 --> 00:57:20.369
So... no.


00:57:20.402 --> 00:57:23.506
Wait. Dream contagion?
Is that like...


00:57:24.540 --> 00:57:26.008
Sometimes in the dreams,
it's like


00:57:26.041 --> 00:57:27.843
she can't completely control
them, like I'm seeing things


00:57:27.877 --> 00:57:30.012
that she wouldn't want me
to see. Like just now,


00:57:30.045 --> 00:57:32.047
I saw you getting ready
to leave for New York.


00:57:34.550 --> 00:57:36.284
Nobody's going anywhere
until we find Charlotte.


00:57:37.720 --> 00:57:38.988
<i>The Craft here will
keep researching.</i>


00:57:39.021 --> 00:57:41.857
You, Mel and the frat boy can...


00:57:44.760 --> 00:57:47.096
- Where's the frat boy?
- That burrito-chomping,


00:57:47.129 --> 00:57:49.632
protein-powder-snorting,
gullible, mush-brained...


00:57:51.567 --> 00:57:53.836
Dope. I told him.


00:57:53.869 --> 00:57:55.738
It's the same as Laf.


00:57:55.771 --> 00:57:58.073
OK. We have to find Charlotte
and get that brooch back


00:57:58.107 --> 00:58:00.109
before Elle finishes
this little re-enactment


00:58:00.142 --> 00:58:02.044
<i>of And Then There Were None.</i>


00:58:02.077 --> 00:58:04.814
<i>Search every nook and cranny.
Charlotte has to be somewhere.</i>


00:58:04.847 --> 00:58:07.550
<i>Be careful. Elle knows
this place better than we ever will.</i>


00:58:36.445 --> 00:58:39.582
"Girls are caterpillars
while they live in the world,


00:58:39.615 --> 00:58:42.985
"to be finally butterflies
when summer comes.


00:58:43.018 --> 00:58:46.589
But in the meantime,
they are grubs and larvae."


00:58:46.622 --> 00:58:48.858
So says Monsieur Le Fanu.


00:58:48.891 --> 00:58:50.960
To think of the trouble
I went to,


00:58:50.993 --> 00:58:52.962
warning you.


00:58:52.995 --> 00:58:55.798
Thinking you'd learn
from my mistake.


00:58:57.766 --> 00:58:59.969
Yeah, 'cause Carm's
the villain here.


00:59:00.002 --> 00:59:03.005
Aren't you the one zapping
innocent people for no reason?


00:59:03.038 --> 00:59:05.007
I'm doing it
to keep what's mine.


00:59:05.040 --> 00:59:07.743
- That life isn't yours.
- It's what I'm owed.


00:59:07.776 --> 00:59:11.413
And I wouldn't waste it
on some banal five-year plan.


00:59:12.548 --> 00:59:13.549
Laf?


00:59:17.620 --> 00:59:20.055
Laf. I saw Laf...


00:59:20.089 --> 00:59:22.191
drawing some kind of symbol.


00:59:22.224 --> 00:59:24.827
It looked like this. Or...


00:59:24.860 --> 00:59:27.663
maybe like... this.


00:59:30.032 --> 00:59:31.834
How did you get
past second grade?


00:59:31.867 --> 00:59:33.202
I saw it for half a second
in a ghost-induced nightmare.


00:59:33.235 --> 00:59:36.138
- Give me a break.
- Any idea what it means?


00:59:36.171 --> 00:59:38.641
No, but...


00:59:38.674 --> 00:59:40.643
if Laf thinks it's
important enough to send


00:59:40.676 --> 00:59:42.144
from beyond the vale...


00:59:42.177 --> 00:59:44.747
If I could just identify it,
maybe it could help decipher


00:59:44.780 --> 00:59:46.749
the moving on spell.
I'll try to figure this out


00:59:46.782 --> 00:59:47.983
- while you guys...
- Go get a life.


00:59:49.685 --> 00:59:51.687
- Go with her. Keep her safe.
- What're you gonna do?


00:59:51.720 --> 00:59:54.823
Well, the young lady
stole my life


00:59:54.857 --> 00:59:56.825
and turned me
back into a vampire.


00:59:56.859 --> 00:59:58.827
So I'm gonna remind her
what that means.


00:59:58.861 --> 01:00:01.764
- How about you?
- Oh, I've got the EMF.


01:00:01.797 --> 01:00:03.799
If it so much as peeps,
I'll shriek.


01:00:37.099 --> 01:00:39.034
I used to think
you and I


01:00:39.068 --> 01:00:40.936
would spend our lives
reading to each other.


01:00:42.738 --> 01:00:45.808
If only I'd known how brief one
of those lives was going to be.


01:00:46.942 --> 01:00:48.610
Hello, Elle.


01:00:53.749 --> 01:00:55.784
Is that all you have
to say to me?


01:00:55.818 --> 01:00:57.853
After what you did?


01:00:57.886 --> 01:01:00.089
I never meant to hurt you.


01:01:01.757 --> 01:01:04.760
Oh... Don't apologize.


01:01:04.793 --> 01:01:06.795
It costs you nothing.


01:01:09.698 --> 01:01:11.667
So what?


01:01:11.700 --> 01:01:13.802
This is about me
paying for my sins?


01:01:14.803 --> 01:01:16.605
You never even stopped


01:01:16.638 --> 01:01:18.273
to think if you
deserve this life.


01:01:19.775 --> 01:01:20.843
I've watched you.


01:01:22.277 --> 01:01:24.613
All these years,


01:01:24.646 --> 01:01:27.649
you've never thought
of anyone but yourself.


01:01:29.118 --> 01:01:30.986
Well, that's some big talk


01:01:31.020 --> 01:01:32.855
coming from the girl


01:01:32.888 --> 01:01:34.790
who sent her friends
to a nightmare land.


01:01:34.823 --> 01:01:36.992
Me?


01:01:37.026 --> 01:01:39.028
Oh, no. I'm just
thinking about myself.


01:01:39.061 --> 01:01:41.764
Oh, wait. I wonder
who taught me that.


01:01:45.300 --> 01:01:47.236
Ooh.


01:01:47.269 --> 01:01:49.571
Not very ladylike,
Miss Karnstein.


01:01:49.605 --> 01:01:52.074
Laura.


01:01:52.107 --> 01:01:54.276
Better run, Carmilla.


01:01:56.311 --> 01:01:59.648
These old houses
are so dangerous, after all.


01:01:59.681 --> 01:02:01.116
Damn it!


01:02:01.150 --> 01:02:04.319
Perry. You never should
have left her alone!


01:02:04.354 --> 01:02:06.155
No sign of the spell
book, either.


01:02:06.188 --> 01:02:08.123
It take it your little chat with
the Ghost of Girlfriends Past


01:02:08.157 --> 01:02:09.992
- was a bust?
- Yeah. I'm getting pretty sick


01:02:10.025 --> 01:02:12.795
- of this haunting crap.
- Imagine how we feel.


01:02:14.897 --> 01:02:17.266
I'm wondering if we might be
of assistance to each other.


01:02:19.101 --> 01:02:21.170
Miss Sheridan said you would
never go along with the spell


01:02:21.203 --> 01:02:23.373
if you knew she was with us.


01:02:23.406 --> 01:02:26.875
I should've known that she only
wanted your life for herself.


01:02:26.909 --> 01:02:29.745
It was all she ever
talked about,


01:02:29.778 --> 01:02:32.081
the wide world
that she'd been denied...


01:02:32.114 --> 01:02:34.950
as if the same thing
hadn't happened to us all.


01:02:38.687 --> 01:02:41.190
I'm sorry about your friend.


01:02:41.223 --> 01:02:43.725
I didn't know what would happen
when they pulled me back.


01:02:44.860 --> 01:02:46.862
Can you help us
get them back?


01:02:50.065 --> 01:02:52.234
I don't know...


01:02:52.267 --> 01:02:54.337
but we have to stop
Miss Sheridan.


01:02:54.370 --> 01:02:56.305
You got any thoughts
on the stopping front?


01:02:58.273 --> 01:03:01.344
It's me she wants,
so perhaps...


01:03:11.887 --> 01:03:14.756
<i>Do we really have to do this
Nightmare on Elm Street crap?</i>


01:03:16.392 --> 01:03:17.393
Fine.


01:03:23.098 --> 01:03:25.100
Let's speak as reasonable women.


01:03:27.903 --> 01:03:29.238
Ahem.


01:03:30.772 --> 01:03:32.375
So...


01:03:32.408 --> 01:03:35.010
your friends are...


01:03:35.043 --> 01:03:36.912
trapped beyond the vale.


01:03:37.913 --> 01:03:39.982
You, Carmilla and your...


01:03:40.015 --> 01:03:42.050
trigger-happy accomplice...


01:03:42.084 --> 01:03:43.252
What next? Sugar?


01:03:44.253 --> 01:03:45.921
Sure.


01:03:48.157 --> 01:03:49.992
But...


01:03:50.025 --> 01:03:52.362
if you hand over Charlotte,


01:03:52.395 --> 01:03:55.764
- and let me keep this life...
- It isn't yours to keep!


01:03:55.797 --> 01:03:57.199
That's beside the point.


01:03:58.834 --> 01:04:02.104
Let me keep it... and I'll bring
your friends back.


01:04:03.439 --> 01:04:06.442
You can all... leave this place.


01:04:12.915 --> 01:04:14.883
What happens to Charlotte?


01:04:14.917 --> 01:04:16.952
Well, I'm afraid


01:04:16.985 --> 01:04:19.788
poor Charlotte will
have to follow her sister,


01:04:19.821 --> 01:04:22.458
but... you know, that was
always going to happen, so.


01:04:22.492 --> 01:04:24.460
She's just like you.


01:04:24.494 --> 01:04:27.296
They all are. Don't they
deserve a chance to move on?


01:04:28.964 --> 01:04:31.401
Oh. Oh...


01:04:33.436 --> 01:04:35.438
You haven't figured it out yet.


01:04:35.471 --> 01:04:37.440
The only way that Charlotte


01:04:37.473 --> 01:04:39.409
and Emily can reach their...


01:04:39.442 --> 01:04:41.143
everlasting rest...


01:04:42.478 --> 01:04:45.747
...is if Carmilla sacrifices
her human life.


01:04:49.552 --> 01:04:51.820
So...


01:04:51.853 --> 01:04:54.122
Let's not pretend that you'd
sacrifice Carmilla's life


01:04:54.156 --> 01:04:56.858
for a few wayward spirits


01:04:56.892 --> 01:04:58.528
- any more than I would.
- We can't just leave them


01:04:58.561 --> 01:05:00.996
- trapped in a nightmare.
- You'd let your friends die


01:05:01.029 --> 01:05:03.333
in here to... help them?


01:05:03.366 --> 01:05:05.867
- There has to be another way!
- Ugh!


01:05:05.901 --> 01:05:07.936
You've had your chance.


01:05:07.970 --> 01:05:10.239
Whatever happens now
is your fault.


01:05:12.274 --> 01:05:14.142
Elle?


01:05:16.346 --> 01:05:18.180
Are you all right?
Did she do anything to you


01:05:18.213 --> 01:05:21.783
- in the dreamscape?
- No.


01:05:23.519 --> 01:05:25.754
No. I just wanna
get her out of my head.


01:05:27.557 --> 01:05:29.525
I wanna get
your life back.


01:05:29.559 --> 01:05:31.994
Well, we think we can lure her
out into the open


01:05:32.027 --> 01:05:34.162
by using Charlotte as bait.


01:05:34.196 --> 01:05:36.298
You'd do that
for us?


01:05:38.334 --> 01:05:40.869
There's only a few hours left
of the Ash Moon.


01:05:40.902 --> 01:05:43.373
If Emily and I
want to move on...


01:05:44.840 --> 01:05:46.842
...it's our only chance.


01:06:04.059 --> 01:06:05.395
There you are!


01:06:06.562 --> 01:06:07.996
You know, it's impolite


01:06:08.030 --> 01:06:10.333
to cause your host
so much trouble.


01:06:10.366 --> 01:06:12.934
I'm sure I'll find a way
to repay you.


01:06:24.547 --> 01:06:26.382
A trap.


01:06:26.416 --> 01:06:28.116
You aren't serious.


01:06:28.150 --> 01:06:30.919
Vampire, warrior,


01:06:30.952 --> 01:06:33.389
journalist... I like
our chances.


01:06:33.423 --> 01:06:35.090
Let's have a little chat


01:06:35.123 --> 01:06:37.192
about taking things
that don't belong to us.


01:06:37.225 --> 01:06:40.430
You first.


01:06:40.463 --> 01:06:43.999
- MEL!
- Ooh! Best get the broom out!


01:06:46.402 --> 01:06:48.003
Look at that.


01:06:49.104 --> 01:06:50.506
Then there were three.


01:06:54.142 --> 01:06:56.311
You should've taken up
my offer, sweetheart.


01:06:56.346 --> 01:06:59.382
- Offer?
- Your life for your friends.


01:06:59.415 --> 01:07:02.117
Don't worry. Laura declined


01:07:02.150 --> 01:07:04.420
when she discovered Charlotte
and Emily can't move on


01:07:04.454 --> 01:07:07.423
without destroying
your... precious spark.


01:07:08.691 --> 01:07:11.427
You'll never be
able to enjoy it.


01:07:11.461 --> 01:07:13.429
You'll spend the rest
of your days


01:07:13.463 --> 01:07:15.365
looking over
your shoulder...


01:07:16.932 --> 01:07:19.435
...wondering if it's my step
you hear at the door.


01:07:24.973 --> 01:07:26.576
I'll take my chances.


01:07:26.609 --> 01:07:28.644
I've got the brooch.


01:07:28.678 --> 01:07:31.046
There's nothing
you can do to stop me.


01:07:31.079 --> 01:07:33.248
Maybe not...
but she knows Krav Maga.


01:07:33.281 --> 01:07:36.652
What?


01:07:38.488 --> 01:07:40.556
Why do people
always forget that?


01:07:47.397 --> 01:07:49.231
NOOO!


01:07:55.170 --> 01:07:57.172
Hello?


01:08:00.142 --> 01:08:01.143
Carm?


01:08:03.145 --> 01:08:04.146
CARM!


01:08:14.189 --> 01:08:16.191
OK.


01:08:19.227 --> 01:08:21.464
Pull yourself together, Hollis.


01:09:08.478 --> 01:09:12.013
Oh, crap. We're live?
Today, on Toronto News 9,


01:09:12.047 --> 01:09:14.316
it's harsh reality.


01:09:14.350 --> 01:09:16.586
Abandon your childhood dreams
for the dubious security


01:09:16.619 --> 01:09:18.788
of a subpar paycheque.


01:09:18.821 --> 01:09:21.156
Spend your days glorifying
clickbait and your nights


01:09:21.189 --> 01:09:22.792
letting fear and misery
drive away friends


01:09:22.825 --> 01:09:25.628
and loved ones. Accept that
life is an unbroken chain


01:09:25.661 --> 01:09:29.665
of mediocrity
stretching on and on and on.


01:09:29.699 --> 01:09:31.601
This is Laura Hollis,


01:09:31.634 --> 01:09:34.337
reporting live
from a failed career.


01:09:34.370 --> 01:09:36.606
I want my life,
you little thief!


01:09:36.639 --> 01:09:38.641
I WANT MY LIFE!


01:09:40.576 --> 01:09:42.512
- Doors are arbitrary.
- You're gonna love New York.


01:09:42.545 --> 01:09:44.480
- Wonderful.
- There's...


01:09:44.514 --> 01:09:46.449
theatre and concerts


01:09:46.482 --> 01:09:48.351
and... life.


01:09:48.384 --> 01:09:51.119
Wait. I know this.
I dreamed this.


01:09:51.152 --> 01:09:53.121
Your life is gonna be so much
bigger than you ever imagined.


01:09:53.154 --> 01:09:55.525
What are you doing?


01:09:55.558 --> 01:09:58.761
You don't belong here!


01:10:08.437 --> 01:10:11.306
She laughed.


01:10:11.340 --> 01:10:14.443
Miss Sheridan, she laughed


01:10:14.477 --> 01:10:16.479
at the very idea of...


01:10:16.512 --> 01:10:20.181
- Oh, God.
- Why did we trust her?


01:10:20.215 --> 01:10:21.817
Poor Emily.


01:10:21.851 --> 01:10:23.653
- Why did we not...
- Poor Charlotte.


01:10:23.686 --> 01:10:25.521
I was supposed


01:10:25.555 --> 01:10:27.356
to keep you safe.


01:10:27.390 --> 01:10:29.625
Do you know what'll happen
if you die in here?


01:10:29.659 --> 01:10:31.627
Let me guess.


01:10:31.661 --> 01:10:33.529
- I die in the real world too.
- Worse.


01:10:33.563 --> 01:10:35.464
You'll be trapped


01:10:35.498 --> 01:10:37.466
in this hell made of dead minds.


01:10:37.500 --> 01:10:40.636
I wonder if you'll feel


01:10:40.670 --> 01:10:43.639
- so sympathetic then.
- Is that what happened to you?


01:10:45.474 --> 01:10:47.777
I don't want your pity.
I want my life!


01:10:50.178 --> 01:10:52.715
I can take it
from you living...


01:10:52.748 --> 01:10:55.283
or I can take it
from you dead.


01:10:55.317 --> 01:10:58.387
You've seen my dreams.


01:10:58.421 --> 01:11:00.389
Have I ever gone down
without a fight?


01:11:07.563 --> 01:11:09.799
Stuck in an endless loop
of someone else's damage.


01:11:09.832 --> 01:11:12.401
- Classic me.
- You're gonna love New York.


01:11:12.435 --> 01:11:15.871
There's... theatre and concerts


01:11:15.905 --> 01:11:17.873
and... life.


01:11:17.907 --> 01:11:20.876
- Oh, God. Carm!
- Your life's gonna be


01:11:20.910 --> 01:11:22.878
so much bigger
than you ever imagined!


01:11:22.912 --> 01:11:25.280
What are you doing?


01:11:37.960 --> 01:11:39.929
I met a woman
in the village today.


01:11:39.962 --> 01:11:43.399
She said strange things
about you.


01:11:48.303 --> 01:11:49.304
What's wrong?


01:11:51.407 --> 01:11:53.542
Why won't you look
at me, Carmilla?


01:11:55.478 --> 01:11:58.313
LOOK AT ME!


01:12:02.752 --> 01:12:04.754
She was right.


01:12:06.722 --> 01:12:09.859
You're a monster.


01:12:09.892 --> 01:12:12.260
I can explain.


01:12:12.293 --> 01:12:14.195
Oh, I've heard
enough of your lies.


01:12:14.229 --> 01:12:16.632
Or your promises.


01:12:16.666 --> 01:12:18.634
All your...


01:12:18.668 --> 01:12:20.670
- talk of a new life!
- No! Not lies.


01:12:20.703 --> 01:12:23.939
In the colonies,
things'll be different!


01:12:23.973 --> 01:12:25.775
No one will know us. You'll see!


01:12:25.808 --> 01:12:27.677
As if I would go anywhere


01:12:27.710 --> 01:12:29.578
with you now.


01:12:29.612 --> 01:12:32.280
No.


01:12:32.313 --> 01:12:34.884
My new friend


01:12:34.917 --> 01:12:38.354
is waiting in a carriage below.


01:12:40.823 --> 01:12:43.258
She's going
to take me traveling.


01:12:43.291 --> 01:12:44.994
She'll show me
the wonders of the world.


01:12:45.027 --> 01:12:46.896
No, you can't go with her.


01:12:48.296 --> 01:12:49.732
Elle, I... I know I lied,


01:12:49.765 --> 01:12:51.934
but... the horror
she has planned for you


01:12:51.967 --> 01:12:53.769
- is much worse than...
- Worse?


01:12:53.803 --> 01:12:56.572
Worse than saying
that she loved me...


01:12:58.674 --> 01:13:00.476
...while she drank my blood?


01:13:01.877 --> 01:13:04.380
WHILE SHE DRANK MY BLOOD?!


01:13:05.481 --> 01:13:06.982
Please...


01:13:11.620 --> 01:13:13.622
Don't worry.


01:13:13.656 --> 01:13:15.858
I've told her
where you are.


01:13:17.026 --> 01:13:20.396
She'll send someone
to deal with you.


01:13:32.808 --> 01:13:34.376
What, is this on repeat?


01:13:35.511 --> 01:13:38.681
How many times
have you watched this?


01:13:40.750 --> 01:13:44.420
It's done. We leave tonight.


01:13:44.453 --> 01:13:46.655
In three days, we'll be on an
ocean liner headed for New York.


01:13:51.527 --> 01:13:53.529
You're gonna love New York.


01:13:53.562 --> 01:13:55.798
There's theatre and concerts


01:13:55.831 --> 01:13:58.834
and... life.


01:13:58.868 --> 01:14:02.071
Oh, your life's gonna be so much
bigger than you ever imagined!


01:14:02.104 --> 01:14:04.406
Hey.


01:14:04.440 --> 01:14:06.442
Hey. It's OK.


01:14:06.475 --> 01:14:09.078
Hey. You are not there anymore.


01:14:09.111 --> 01:14:11.814
You are here with me. Right now.


01:14:13.816 --> 01:14:15.618
And I have the brooch.


01:14:15.651 --> 01:14:17.953
Maybe you can just... absorb it.


01:14:23.759 --> 01:14:25.795
Nothing.


01:14:25.828 --> 01:14:27.763
Of course not.


01:14:27.797 --> 01:14:30.099
Of course we still
need some stupid spell!


01:14:30.132 --> 01:14:32.468
Maybe I should
give her my life.


01:14:34.637 --> 01:14:36.639
What?


01:14:40.576 --> 01:14:43.579
- Carm, you can't. She's unhinged!
- Not to her...


01:14:44.914 --> 01:14:45.915
To them.


01:14:48.083 --> 01:14:50.352
Laura, everything
you saw in there...


01:14:50.386 --> 01:14:53.022
it's everything I've
been avoiding for years.


01:14:55.457 --> 01:14:57.793
Pretending like... being human


01:14:57.827 --> 01:14:59.795
meant I didn't do


01:14:59.829 --> 01:15:02.064
all of those awful things.


01:15:05.835 --> 01:15:08.370
How is it fair
that I get this life


01:15:08.404 --> 01:15:10.472
while they're just
trapped here?


01:15:12.842 --> 01:15:14.910
After everything
I have done?


01:15:18.180 --> 01:15:20.149
OK.


01:15:20.182 --> 01:15:22.384
OK.


01:15:22.418 --> 01:15:24.620
A...


01:15:24.653 --> 01:15:26.388
let's acknowledge
that Ellen, your mother,


01:15:26.422 --> 01:15:29.124
shares some of this
blame, and B...


01:15:29.158 --> 01:15:31.126
we will figure out
another way,


01:15:31.160 --> 01:15:33.462
a way that doesn't involve
you giving up your life.


01:15:33.495 --> 01:15:35.965
You mean, find a way
to avoid responsibility?


01:15:37.600 --> 01:15:39.602
Hm-mm.


01:15:39.635 --> 01:15:41.070
You heard Elle...


01:15:42.805 --> 01:15:44.874
...there's no other way.


01:15:44.907 --> 01:15:46.876
It's my life
for their freedom.


01:15:46.909 --> 01:15:48.777
What about
our life together?


01:15:50.512 --> 01:15:52.114
Our future?


01:15:54.683 --> 01:15:57.052
You're just gonna
give up on that?


01:15:57.086 --> 01:15:59.822
- Laura, I'm not giving up...
- 'Cause we're supposed to have


01:15:59.855 --> 01:16:02.625
arguments over who does dishes,
and cupcakes to celebrate


01:16:02.658 --> 01:16:05.728
big days at work
and grandkids.


01:16:08.564 --> 01:16:09.999
What is that gonna look like
if you can live


01:16:10.032 --> 01:16:12.001
like you're 25 forever?


01:16:13.669 --> 01:16:17.573
You think I don't want
those things, too?


01:16:17.606 --> 01:16:20.042
Please don't give up
on our life.


01:16:20.075 --> 01:16:23.112
I'm not giving up.


01:16:25.114 --> 01:16:28.784
But I can't keep running away.


01:16:28.817 --> 01:16:31.553
Not after what I've done.


01:16:34.757 --> 01:16:36.725
OK.


01:16:46.802 --> 01:16:48.637
Thank you.


01:16:54.677 --> 01:16:57.780
Let's go save some ghosts.


01:17:11.627 --> 01:17:13.696
Seriously?


01:17:13.729 --> 01:17:15.764
People can't just dream
about getting audited?


01:17:20.703 --> 01:17:21.670
Laf!


01:17:26.241 --> 01:17:28.210
- How did you...?
- Escape my personal hell.


01:17:28.243 --> 01:17:30.212
I've been through
like three apocalypses,


01:17:30.245 --> 01:17:32.681
- I can tell the difference.
- You found any of the others?


01:17:35.751 --> 01:17:37.519
Funny you should mention that.


01:17:39.121 --> 01:17:41.724
I've been trying to wake her,
but she keeps mistaking me


01:17:41.757 --> 01:17:44.126
for... me.


01:17:44.159 --> 01:17:46.962
Form 83-B done.


01:17:48.764 --> 01:17:52.034
- Filing a 100 of these daily.
- You don't mind taking care


01:17:52.067 --> 01:17:54.203
of the deeds, right? It'll just
be like 5 or 6 million pages.


01:17:54.236 --> 01:17:57.272
You can do this alone; you don't
need me. See you in 6 years.


01:18:00.242 --> 01:18:02.578
Laura.


01:18:02.611 --> 01:18:04.680
What... are you
doing in my...


01:18:04.713 --> 01:18:06.682
strangely bureaucratic
nightmare?


01:18:06.715 --> 01:18:08.717
Elle zapped us
into nightmare land.


01:18:08.751 --> 01:18:10.719
We have to do the spell
before sunrise,


01:18:10.753 --> 01:18:12.921
- which is coming up fast.
- Well, I...


01:18:12.955 --> 01:18:15.190
I had to weigh the pages
before Elle zapped me,


01:18:15.224 --> 01:18:17.593
but without the code key
to decipher the spell...


01:18:17.626 --> 01:18:19.061
I've got the code key.


01:18:20.929 --> 01:18:24.066
Oh! Yes, the symbol!
Do you have the full thing?


01:18:24.099 --> 01:18:27.269
Uh, yeah, I literally
have a photographic memory.


01:18:27.302 --> 01:18:30.906
Oh, I could
just kiss you


01:18:30.939 --> 01:18:32.941
in your robot eye.


01:18:40.350 --> 01:18:42.684
You're safe.


01:18:46.889 --> 01:18:49.191
Why are people always
hunting me for sport?


01:18:51.226 --> 01:18:53.228
And Mrs. Sheridan,


01:18:53.262 --> 01:18:55.297
she laughed at the very idea...


01:19:15.951 --> 01:19:18.087
OK, circle up.
We don't need


01:19:18.120 --> 01:19:21.256
to hold hands or anything,
the spell is much more powerful,


01:19:21.290 --> 01:19:24.360
but you might be
more cozy that way.


01:19:24.394 --> 01:19:26.662
So what happens to us
after the ghosts move on?


01:19:26.695 --> 01:19:29.264
Oh, hmm...


01:19:29.298 --> 01:19:31.800
<i>Well, we'll either find
ourselves back at the schloss.</i>


01:19:31.834 --> 01:19:34.703
- or cease to exist entirely.
- Better than our usual lots.


01:19:34.736 --> 01:19:37.806
I'm sorry. Not to criticise
any plan that would clearly


01:19:37.840 --> 01:19:40.343
- be so much to our benefit, but...
- Doesn't that mean


01:19:40.376 --> 01:19:42.311
you have to give up
your human life?


01:19:44.313 --> 01:19:47.350
Yeah.
Well, I'm responsible


01:19:47.383 --> 01:19:49.785
for what happened to you,


01:19:49.818 --> 01:19:52.721
so... this is how
I can help.


01:19:59.027 --> 01:20:00.929
- Whoa! What happened to the...?
- It's a cake now.


01:20:00.963 --> 01:20:03.866
- Don't ask.
- OK.


01:20:03.899 --> 01:20:06.201
Alright, uh, let's get
this ritual started


01:20:06.235 --> 01:20:07.703
before I change my mind.


01:20:23.719 --> 01:20:26.422
Carm!


01:20:28.090 --> 01:20:30.792
You think I'm gonna
let you do this?


01:20:30.826 --> 01:20:32.761
- Steal everything from me again?!
- But Carm really isn't


01:20:32.794 --> 01:20:34.830
the one you blame for that.


01:20:34.863 --> 01:20:37.166
Is she?
I've seen that moment


01:20:37.199 --> 01:20:39.168
between you two
over and over again.


01:20:39.201 --> 01:20:41.203
You had everything that you ever
wanted and you gave it up


01:20:41.236 --> 01:20:43.272
- because you were afraid.
- They lied to me.


01:20:43.305 --> 01:20:45.207
Carmilla, her mother,


01:20:45.240 --> 01:20:47.242
they betrayed
and murdered me!


01:20:47.276 --> 01:20:48.911
You're right: it isn't fair
what happened to you,


01:20:48.944 --> 01:20:50.913
but that's not an excuse.


01:20:50.946 --> 01:20:53.849
Everything that you're
doing right now -


01:20:53.882 --> 01:20:55.751
hurting everyone else, hurting
yourself - it's just because


01:20:55.784 --> 01:20:57.819
you're afraid of what comes
next, but you don't have to be.


01:20:57.853 --> 01:20:59.254
We can help you.


01:20:59.288 --> 01:21:01.256
We can help you find the peace
that you've always been


01:21:01.290 --> 01:21:03.025
- looking for.
- No!


01:21:03.058 --> 01:21:05.961
No, I don't want
your platitudes! I want my...


01:21:08.498 --> 01:21:12.000
Your life.
You want your life.


01:21:12.034 --> 01:21:14.370
- Yeah, we know.
- Ugh!


01:21:14.404 --> 01:21:18.106
But it's not all about you.
And you're a part


01:21:18.140 --> 01:21:20.476
of this. Stay put.


01:21:20.510 --> 01:21:22.811
- Nice shot!
- I've been waiting to do that


01:21:22.844 --> 01:21:24.414
since we got here.


01:21:26.915 --> 01:21:28.884
So, you're kind of rocking
the field work these days, huh?


01:21:28.917 --> 01:21:31.987
Think if we got some more
admin help, you'd be able


01:21:32.020 --> 01:21:35.023
- to come out more.
- I think I could


01:21:35.057 --> 01:21:37.059
find some time to play.


01:21:39.362 --> 01:21:41.730
We're almost free
of all of this.


01:21:43.533 --> 01:21:46.134
You shouldn't have been
drawn into it to begin with.


01:21:46.168 --> 01:21:49.238
It was 1872.


01:21:49.271 --> 01:21:51.106
If we hadn't been
killed by vampires,


01:21:51.139 --> 01:21:53.008
it would have been...


01:21:53.041 --> 01:21:55.010
I don't know, tuberculosis?


01:21:55.043 --> 01:21:57.279
Oddly specific.


01:21:59.349 --> 01:22:01.316
Each day was made better


01:22:01.351 --> 01:22:04.520
because you tried
to make it such.


01:22:04.554 --> 01:22:06.788
I don't regret a thing.


01:22:12.227 --> 01:22:14.162
Thank you...


01:22:14.196 --> 01:22:16.231
for the dance.


01:22:16.265 --> 01:22:18.468
I wish there could
be another, but...


01:22:18.501 --> 01:22:20.470
I get it.


01:22:20.503 --> 01:22:22.938
You gotta leave
with the one that brung you.


01:22:25.173 --> 01:22:27.209
Would you like to...?


01:22:28.578 --> 01:22:30.279
Obviously.


01:22:43.225 --> 01:22:46.429
Ugh, can we please
just move on already?


01:23:07.316 --> 01:23:10.218
Ah, it's working!


01:23:39.649 --> 01:23:41.917
What the hell now?


01:23:44.554 --> 01:23:46.522
Guess with all
the ghosts gone,


01:23:46.556 --> 01:23:49.659
there's no reason for this place
to exist anymore.


01:23:49.692 --> 01:23:52.395
So...


01:23:52.428 --> 01:23:54.196
it worked.


01:23:54.229 --> 01:23:55.964
Hurray.


01:24:00.202 --> 01:24:02.270
Sorry about before.


01:24:04.039 --> 01:24:06.642
I think I've been so focused
on chasing after your life


01:24:06.676 --> 01:24:08.944
'cause it seemed
a lot easier than...


01:24:08.977 --> 01:24:11.079
trying to fix my own.


01:24:11.113 --> 01:24:13.148
Hey...


01:24:15.150 --> 01:24:17.387
...you're Laura Hollis.


01:24:19.054 --> 01:24:21.557
...and I have
watched you fight


01:24:21.591 --> 01:24:25.060
vampires and... gods,


01:24:25.093 --> 01:24:28.163
and even that lady
who tried to butt us in line


01:24:28.196 --> 01:24:30.232
at the craft fair.


01:24:32.234 --> 01:24:34.970
So you're gonna
figure it out.


01:24:35.003 --> 01:24:37.105
Whatever happens next...


01:24:39.375 --> 01:24:41.411
...we're gonna
do it together.


01:24:49.317 --> 01:24:51.286
This goes Romeo
and Juliet on us,


01:24:51.319 --> 01:24:53.321
I'm totally gonna
haunt your ass.


01:24:55.190 --> 01:24:57.225
Of course you are.


01:25:21.584 --> 01:25:23.719
Well, that was a kick.


01:25:27.757 --> 01:25:29.725
<i>Where are you, guys?</i>


01:25:29.759 --> 01:25:31.993
<i>Is everyone OK? Over.</i>


01:25:34.162 --> 01:25:38.367
Affirmative.
Laura and Carm A-OK.


01:25:38.401 --> 01:25:40.570
<i>- Over.
- Front door is unlocked.</i>


01:25:40.603 --> 01:25:43.205
<i>Oh! Meet you outside.</i>


01:25:43.238 --> 01:25:45.374
<i>- You're supposed to say over.
- Over.</i>


01:25:47.677 --> 01:25:49.679
Let's get the hell out
of Styria.


01:26:10.800 --> 01:26:12.768
I call dibs on window!


01:26:43.833 --> 01:26:45.735
Hmm...


01:26:45.768 --> 01:26:47.770
and how does it feel,
Ms. Hollis,


01:26:47.803 --> 01:26:51.239
to officially be
a freelance journalist at large?


01:26:51.273 --> 01:26:53.776
I've made a huge mistake!
What have I done?


01:26:53.809 --> 01:26:56.679
I quit my job.
I gave up my cubicle!


01:26:56.712 --> 01:26:59.281
I don't have a plan! What am I
supposed to do without a plan?


01:27:01.316 --> 01:27:03.352
Only about half of that
was actual panic,


01:27:03.386 --> 01:27:05.755
- so pretty good, right?
- Yeah.


01:27:07.222 --> 01:27:08.691
I'm just gonna go
get some blood, babe.


01:27:12.395 --> 01:27:15.364
- So this is a blueprint?
- Yep, the blueprints


01:27:15.398 --> 01:27:18.199
they sent over.
And, oh, check this out.


01:27:18.233 --> 01:27:20.369
They have an industrial-size
cleaning closet.


01:27:20.403 --> 01:27:22.638
And then I was thinking we could
put your reactor over here,


01:27:22.672 --> 01:27:24.640
- in this corner.
- That is a beautiful thing.


01:27:24.674 --> 01:27:26.642
Selling out
going smoothly?


01:27:26.676 --> 01:27:28.744
Uh, we're retaining
executive control


01:27:28.778 --> 01:27:31.179
over Laferry at Intrigue.
And they're giving us


01:27:31.212 --> 01:27:34.249
a thorium reactor.
A thorium reactor!


01:27:34.282 --> 01:27:36.752
- It was really scary.
- It sounds a little cushy.


01:27:36.786 --> 01:27:38.788
But it was a totally
legit adventure.


01:27:38.821 --> 01:27:40.790
You know, there were ghosts
and a haunted mansion,


01:27:40.823 --> 01:27:42.792
and then, you know,
this weird netherworld.


01:27:42.825 --> 01:27:44.894
And comfy beds
and midnight snacks,


01:27:44.927 --> 01:27:48.331
- and a masquerade ball.
- Look, I even have a mark


01:27:48.364 --> 01:27:50.333
where I got ghost zapped. Look.


01:27:50.366 --> 01:27:52.335
- No, seriously, look.
- No, I see it.


01:27:52.368 --> 01:27:54.337
- That's good.
- Look! It's there, look!


01:27:54.370 --> 01:27:56.772
- You can put it away now.
- OK, don't give me


01:27:56.806 --> 01:27:59.542
pity eyes, Hollis.
Like, you never had a crush


01:27:59.575 --> 01:28:02.511
- on a dead girl...
- That does sound familiar.


01:28:05.748 --> 01:28:07.416
Thanks.


01:28:13.656 --> 01:28:16.157
So...


01:28:16.191 --> 01:28:18.159
- Carmilla Karnstein...
- Hmmm...


01:28:18.193 --> 01:28:20.496
...a vampire again.


01:28:20.529 --> 01:28:22.665
What's next?


01:28:22.698 --> 01:28:26.569
I'm thinking...
maybe my PhD in Philosophy.


01:28:28.437 --> 01:28:30.873
Hey, attend university
for 70-odd years


01:28:30.906 --> 01:28:33.409
and you rack up
a few credits.


01:28:33.442 --> 01:28:35.945
So proud of you.


01:28:35.978 --> 01:28:37.713
You're not worried
about how we'll spend


01:28:37.747 --> 01:28:39.180
the rest of our lives together?


01:28:41.216 --> 01:28:43.719
I figure any two people
in a relationship,


01:28:43.753 --> 01:28:46.287
their lives move
at different paces.


01:28:46.321 --> 01:28:49.625
That isn't the part
that matters.


01:28:50.626 --> 01:28:51.761
This...


01:28:52.762 --> 01:28:54.730
...here...


01:28:54.764 --> 01:28:56.632
right now...


01:28:56.666 --> 01:28:59.602
This is what matters.


01:28:59.635 --> 01:29:01.671
And I love you.


01:29:04.272 --> 01:29:06.241
I love you too.


01:29:25.326 --> 01:29:27.663
I'm Laura Hollis


01:29:27.697 --> 01:29:30.533
and this is a web exclusive
for Cream Puffington Post.


01:29:30.566 --> 01:29:32.968
We're talking today
with veteran dragonslayer


01:29:33.002 --> 01:29:37.606
Elizabeth Spielsdorf about
the great apocalypse of 2015.


01:29:37.640 --> 01:29:39.875
Hi, I'm Laura Hollis
on assignment in Graz


01:29:39.909 --> 01:29:42.011
where we're just in time
for the ribbon cutting ceremony


01:29:42.044 --> 01:29:44.780
on the J.P. Armitage
Memorial Library.


01:29:44.814 --> 01:29:46.782
I'm Laura Hollis
reporting to you live


01:29:46.816 --> 01:29:49.317
from the Geneva Summit
on the rights of Werepeople.


01:29:49.351 --> 01:29:52.421
I'm Laura Hollis reporting
to you live from Iceland


01:29:52.455 --> 01:29:54.890
where scientists have recently
made a breakthrough discovery


01:29:54.924 --> 01:29:56.892
of the first drinkable
fountain of youth.


01:29:56.926 --> 01:29:59.895
A scandal brewing tonight
on the step of the capital.


01:29:59.929 --> 01:30:02.297
as the President
who, last month, was revealed


01:30:02.331 --> 01:30:05.668
to be an as-yet unidentified
species of lizard creature


01:30:05.701 --> 01:30:08.571
with very small hands
refuses to produce


01:30:08.604 --> 01:30:10.573
his long-form
hatching certificate.


01:30:10.606 --> 01:30:13.943
This is senior correspondent
Laura Hollis


01:30:13.976 --> 01:30:16.311
for MSSSN-BCD.


01:33:39.682 --> 01:33:41.850
Hey, Maddie.


01:33:41.884 --> 01:33:44.486
Hey, sis.


01:33:44.520 --> 01:33:46.522
- What are you...?
- Back from the underworld


01:33:46.555 --> 01:33:50.659
and lounging in your charmingly
Bohemian pied-a-terre.


01:33:50.693 --> 01:33:53.262
For starters.


01:33:53.295 --> 01:33:56.231
You and I and the little
ingénue that could


01:33:56.265 --> 01:33:58.934
are going on a road trip.


01:33:58.968 --> 01:34:02.972
Turns out the angler fish
was female.


01:34:03.005 --> 01:34:05.808
Before it died, it laid eggs.


01:34:05.841 --> 01:34:09.979
Just an alarming
